f FY2024 sales came from aftermarket and approximately 90% from proprietary products; it characterizes aftermarket revenues as historically higher gross profit and more stable than OEM sales. These remain Management Language, not independently established competitive statistics. Long aircraft/product lives and qualification investments can slow switching and sustain replacement demand, creating pricing discretion and earnings visibility. However, a proprietary design is not automatically sole-source, and installed-base opportunity is not backlog. Predominantly point-in-time recognition makes shipments and control transfer relevant to realized revenue. Basis: CP-1A B03/B04/B08/B09 and CT01; inherited S1 pp.4, 7, 9, 120\u2013121.","table_display":"Revenue durability and competition. Management estimates approximately 55% of FY2024 sales came from aftermarket and approximately 90% from proprietary products; it characterizes aftermarket revenues as historically higher gross profit and more stable than OEM sales. These remain Management Language, not independently established competitive statistics. Long aircraft/product lives and qualification investments can slow switching and sustain replacement demand, creating pricing discretion and earnings visibility. However, a proprietary design is not automatically sole-source, and installed-base opportunity is not backlog. Predominantly point-in-time recognition makes shipments and control transfer relevant to realized revenue. Basis: CP-1A B03/B04/B08/B09 and CT01; inherited S1 pp.4, 7, 9, 120\u2013121."},{"fact_id":"prose-CP-2-5.r2.c0","label":"Business, ownership and operating economics","table_id":"prose-CP-2-5","row_id":"r2","field":"c0","amount":null,"text":"Price, volume and mix. Value-based pricing is management's stated approach, not a quantified FY2024 price contribution. Utilization, fleet age/size, airline economics, OEM production schedules and defense budgets are supported volume mechanisms (B09/B10). Pricing can