d operating economics","table_id":"prose-CP-2-5","row_id":"r5","field":"c0","amount":null,"text":"Cash conversion. CP-1 CF22, K03 and K12 show stronger operating cash generation and a smaller annual cash use in the complete changes-in-assets/liabilities block in FY2024. Inventory, receivables and unbilled performance can still absorb cash before collection; advance receipts provide partial offsets (CP-1A B13/CT02). Interest, taxes, integration costs, acquisition spend and distributions prevent adjusted EBITDA or annual CFO less capex from representing freely distributable cash. CP-1's ordinary EBITDA and EBITDA As Defined are different reported non-GAAP measures; neither is automatically accepted economic earnings or legal EBITDA.","status":"known","unit":null,"currency":null,"scale":"1","decimals":null,"period":null,"basis":"Literal wrapped paragraph from the model-authored handoff; no new analysis.","denominator":null,"citations":[{"source_id":"CP-2","source_sha256":"46cca7cd74c612c8c29b7d89c572a46c1e86481a387bd1301525e3e440b3ae1c","locator":"line 72","quote":"**Cash conversion.** CP-1 CF22, K03 and K12 show stronger operating cash generation and a smaller annual cash use in the complete changes-in-assets/liabilities block in FY2024. Inventory, receivables and unbilled performance can still absorb cash before collection; advance receipts provide partial offsets (CP-1A B13/CT02). Interest, taxes, integration costs, acquisition spend and distributions prevent adjusted EBITDA or annual CFO less capex from representing freely distributable cash. CP-1's ordinary EBITDA and EBITDA As Defined are different reported non-GAAP measures; neither is automatically accepted economic earnings or legal EBITDA."}],"calculation_id":null,"value_class":"source","source_amount":null,"stated_amount":null,"calculation_status":null,"formula":null,"limitation":null,"display":"Cash conversion. CP-1 CF22, K03 and K12 show stronger operating cash generation and a smaller annual cash use in t