family register. Each numbered family has its own boundary, conditions and missing inputs; the supplementary registers retain capacity, remedies and structural detail. Quoted thresholds are contractual terms, not measured results. No missing usage is treated as zero.","table_display":"This is the clause-specific 14-family register. Each numbered family has its own boundary, conditions and missing inputs; the supplementary registers retain capacity, remedies and structural detail. Quoted thresholds are contractual terms, not measured results. No missing usage is treated as zero."},{"fact_id":"prose-CP-4-6.r0.c0","label":"Legal risks and protections","table_id":"prose-CP-4-6","row_id":"r0","field":"c0","amount":null,"text":"Definitions change capacity, not just reported leverage. L p.5 L410\u2013L424 defines FCCR as legal EBITDA over Fixed Charges for four full quarters with internal statements, pro forma financing and acquisitions/dispositions, transaction-date floating rates and swap effects. Fixed Charges adds tax-grossed preferred dividends to defined interest. Defined interest excludes financing-fee amortization, bridge/commitment fees, qualified securitization costs and prepayment premiums, while adding capitalized interest and capital-lease interest. EBITDA includes expansive transaction, restructuring, dividend-equivalent and projected-savings adjustments. Clause M's 35% limit is neither a global cap on all EBITDA add-backs nor a cap on every pro forma acquisition adjustment: L421\u2013L422 separately permits officer-good-faith acquisition calculations and reasonably determined operating expense reductions. The no-duplication and specified exclusions still matter; the document is not permission to add the same amount twice. Wider earnings and narrower fixed charges can make ratio debt and distributions easier before actual cash savings arrive, increasing debt-service sensitivity and weakening the residual asset cushion. Monitor adjustment categories, actual realization and transaction-date rate inputs, not the accounting multiple.","status":"known","unit":null,"currency":null,"scale":"1","decimals":null,"period":null,"basis":"Literal wrapped paragraph from the model-authored handoff; no new analysis.","denominator":null,"citations":[{"source_id":"CP-4","source_sha256":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e","locator":"line 89","quote":"**Definitions change capacity, not just reported leverage.** L p.5 L410\u2013L424 defines FCCR as legal EBITDA over Fixed Charges for four full quarters with internal statements, pro forma financing and acquisitions/dispositions, transaction-date floating rates and swap effects. Fixed Charges adds tax-grossed preferred dividends to defined interest. Defined interest excludes financing-fee amortization, bridge/commitment fees, qualified securitization costs and prepayment premiums, while adding capitalized interest and capital-lease interest. EBITDA includes expansive transaction, restructuring, dividend-equivalent and projected-savings adjustments. Clause M's 35% limit is neither a global cap on all EBITDA add-backs nor a cap on every pro forma acquisition adjustment: L421\u2013L422 separately permits officer-good-faith acquisition calculations and reasonably determined operating expense reductions. The no-duplication and specified exclusions still matter; the document is not permission to add the same amount twice. Wider earnings and narrower fixed charges can make ratio debt and distributions easier before actual cash savings arrive, increasing debt-service sensitivity and weakening the residual asset cushion. Monitor adjustment categories, actual realization and transaction-date rate inputs, not the accounting multiple."}],"calculation_id":null,"value_class":"source","source_amount":null,"stated_amount":null,"calculation_status":null,"formula":null,"limitation":null,"display":"Definitions change capacity, not just reported leverage. L p.5 L410\u2013L424 define