in CP-1A BF01 as extraction behavior, not unlawful payment or coercive LME evidence.","table_display":"The historical distribution demonstrates willingness, not a capacity opinion. S1 p.131 expressly links September notes and Tranche L proceeds plus existing cash to the USD75/share declaration and eligible option equivalents. S1 p.146 records USD4,216 million common dividends accrued at September 30 and USD4,216 million common plus USD132 million equivalent payments in October 2024. The latter are subsequent cash uses, not FY2024 cash flow. Neither the funding link nor the issuer compliance statement on p.132 identifies the precise \u00a74.07 route, verifies conditions at declaration/commitment or proves residual capacity. A general compliance assertion is not the missing transaction certificate. Retain CP-1A BF01 as extraction behavior, not unlawful payment or coercive LME evidence."},{"fact_id":"prose-CP-4-6.r4.c0","label":"Legal risks and protections","table_id":"prose-CP-4-6","row_id":"r4","field":"c0","amount":null,"text":"Asset-sale protection is real but delayed and qualified. FMV consideration and conditional cash requirements, reinvestment/application deadlines, and a pro rata 100%-plus-interest offer protect noteholders where \u00a74.10 applies. Countervailing flexibility includes deemed cash (assumed liabilities, instruments converted within 180 days and designated noncash consideration), long reinvestment periods, net-proceeds deductions, use to repay secured or non-guarantor debt, and return of untendered residual to permitted general purposes. The special productive-assets alternative requires substitute Productive Assets promptly to become Collateral where sold assets were collateral (L1317). This supports collateral continuity in that path, but is not a universal requirement that all proceeds immediately repay these Notes. Do not collapse asset-sales proceeds into near-term note amortization.","status":"known","unit":null,"currency":null,"scale":"1","decimals":null,"period":null,"basis":"Literal wrapped paragraph from the model-authored handoff; no new analysis.","denominator":null,"citations":[{"source_id":"CP-4","source_sha256":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e","locator":"line 97","quote":"**Asset-sale protection is real but delayed and qualified.** FMV consideration and conditional cash requirements, reinvestment/application deadlines, and a pro rata 100%-plus-interest offer protect noteholders where \u00a74.10 applies. Countervailing flexibility includes deemed cash (assumed liabilities, instruments converted within 180 days and designated noncash consideration), long reinvestment periods, net-proceeds deductions, use to repay secured or non-guarantor debt, and return of untendered residual to permitted general purposes. The special productive-assets alternative requires substitute Productive Assets promptly to become Collateral where sold assets were collateral (L1317). This supports collateral continuity in that path, but is not a universal requirement that all proceeds immediately repay these Notes. Do not collapse asset-sales proceeds into near-term note amortization."}],"calculation_id":null,"value_class":"source","source_amount":null,"stated_amount":null,"calculation_status":null,"formula":null,"limitation":null,"display":"Asset-sale protection is real but delayed and qualified. FMV consideration and conditional cash requirements, reinvestment/application deadlines, and a pro rata 100%-plus-interest offer protect noteholders where \u00a74.10 applies. Countervailing flexibility includes deemed cash (assumed liabilities, instruments converted within 180 days and designated noncash consideration), long reinvestment periods, net-proceeds deductions, use to repay secured or non-guarantor debt, and return of untendered residual to permitted general purposes. The special productive-assets alternative requires substitute Productive Assets promptly to become Collateral where sold assets were collateral (L1317). This supports collateral continuity in that path, but is not a universal requirement that all proceeds immediately repay these Notes. Do not collapse asset-sales proceeds into near-term note amortization.","table_display":"Asset-sale protection is real but delayed and qualified. FMV consideration and conditional cash requirements, reinvestment/application deadlines, and a pro rata 100%-plus-interest offer protect noteholders where \u00a74.10 applies. Countervailing flexibility includes deemed cash (assumed liabilities, instruments converted within 180 days and designated noncash consideration), long reinvestment periods, net-proceeds deductions, use to repay secured or non-guarantor debt, and return of untendered residual to permitted general purposes. The special productive-assets alternative requires substitute Productive Assets promptly to become Collateral where sold assets were collateral (L1317). This supports collateral continuity in that path, but is not a universal requirement that all proceeds immediately repay these Notes. Do not collapse asset-sales proceeds into near-term note amortization."},{"fact_id":"prose-CP-4-6.r5.c0","label":"Legal risks and protections","table_id":"prose-CP-4-6","row_id":"r5","field":"c0","amount":null,"text":"Guarantees improve direct recourse but are neither universal nor permanent. \u00a710.01 promises unconditional, irrevocable, joint-and-several payment/performance, not merely collection, with reinstatement for rescinded payments; \u00a710.02 limits enforceability by fraudulent-transfer law. The executed signer list includes CPI, Calspan, Raptor entities and TransDigm UK, among others (L pp.31\u201332), but is not a current exhaustive ownership/value schedule. \u00a74.17's facility limb and separate >=200 capital-markets limb can capture new obligors, with 20-Business-Day accession; \u00a712.04 links required guarantee accession to security/ICA joinder. \u00a710.07 nonetheless releases on 