sh, and nominal A/R capacity 650 less drawn is not certified availability. Carrying leverage remains an accounting analytical ratio, not principal-based recovery coverage or legal headroom."},{"fact_id":"prose-CP-3-10.r0.c0","label":"Downside, loss mechanisms and strongest countercases","table_id":"prose-CP-3-10","row_id":"r0","field":"c0","amount":null,"text":"Time-aware operating downside: from the September 2024 base, weaker utilization or qualified-supplier disruption first reduces spares demand or deliverable shipments (CP-1A B10/B11/B14), then revenue/mix and margin (B04/B08), then collections and inventory conversion (B13; CP-1 K03). Interest, reinvestment and committed payouts compete for cash. Borrowing may initially bridge cash needs but raises claims; eligible A/R may tighten just when liquidity is needed. A July 2025 renewal requirement can matter before longer bond maturities, but no outcome is inferred from the missing follow-up. Notes need not suffer an immediate numerical maintenance breach simply because earnings fall. Transaction incurrence/RP permissions, payment default rules and refinancing access are distinct pathways (CP-4 F01/F13).","status":"known","unit":null,"currency":null,"scale":"1","decimals":null,"period":null,"basis":"Literal wrapped paragraph from the model-authored handoff; no new analysis.","denominator":null,"citations":[{"source_id":"CP-3","source_sha256":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7","locator":"line 146","quote":"**Time-aware operating downside:** from the September 2024 base, weaker utilization or qualified-supplier disruption first reduces spares demand or deliverable shipments (CP-1A B10/B11/B14), then revenue/mix and margin (B04/B08), then collections and inventory conversion (B13; CP-1 K03). Interest, reinvestment and committed payouts compete for cash. Borrowing may initially bridge cash needs but raises claims; eligible A/R may tighten just when liquidity is needed. A July 2025 renewal requirement can matter before longer bond maturities, but no outcome is inferred from the missing follow-up. Notes need not suffer an immediate numerical maintenance breach simply because earnings fall. Transaction incurrence/RP permissions, payment default rules and refinancing access are distinct pathways (CP-4 F01/F13)."}],"calculation_id":null,"value_class":"source","source_amount":null,"stated_amount":null,"calculation_status":null,"formula":null,"limitation":null,"display":"Time-aware operating downside: from the September 2024 base, weaker utilization or qualified-supplier disruption first reduces spares demand or deliverable shipments (CP-1A B10/B11/B14), then revenue/mix and margin (B04/B08), then collections and inventory conversion (B13; CP-1 K03). Interest, reinvestment and committed payouts compete for cash. Borrowing may initially bridge cash needs but raises claims; eligible A/R may tighten just when liquidity is needed. A July 2025 renewal requirement can matter before longer bond maturities, but no outcome is inferred from the missing follow-up. Notes need not suffer an immediate numerical maintenance breach simply because earnings fall. Transaction incurrence/RP permissions, payment default rules and refinancing access are distinct pathways (CP-4 F01/F13).","table_display":"Time-aware operating downside: from the September 2024 base, weaker utilization or qualified-supplier disruption first reduces spares demand or deliverable shipments (CP-1A B10/B11/B14), then revenue/mix and margin (B04/B08), then collections and inventory conversion (B13; CP-1 K03). Interest, reinvestment and committed payouts compete for cash. Borrowing may initially bridge cash needs but raises claims; eligible A/R may tighten just when liquidity is needed. A July 2025 renewal requirement can matter before longer bond maturities, but no outcome is inferred from the missing follow-up. Notes need not suffer an immediate numerical maintenance breach simply because earnings fall. Transaction incurrence/RP permissions, payment default rules and refinancing access are distinct pathways (CP-4 F01/F13)."},{"fact_id":"prose-CP-3-10.r1.c0","label":"Downside, loss mechanisms and strongest countercases","table_id":"prose-CP-3-10","row_id":"r1","field":"c0","amount":null,"text":"Economic loss versus legal loss: spread widening or rates rising can create mark-to-market loss before any default. Fixed longer notes face duration plus credit-spread repricing; floating loans can have less fixed-rate duration but credit discount and exit-liquidity risk, while higher floating service costs affect issuer cash. In a later restructuring, lower enterprise/pool values, senior dilution, leakage, costs and realization delay reduce distributable proceeds; subordination makes juniors more convex to residual shortfall. A bond's par shortfall is not the investor's entry-price loss: economic loss depends on purchase price, proceeds, interim cash and timing, all of which are missing here. No assumed recovery floor, stress magnitude, PD or portfolio loss is assigned.","status":"known","unit":null,"currency":null,"scale":"1","decimals":null,"period":null,"basis":"Literal wrapped paragraph from the model-authored handoff; no new analysis.","denominator":null,"citations":[{"source_id":"CP-3","source_sha256":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7","locator":"line 148","quote":"**Economic loss versus legal loss:** spread widening or rates rising can create mark-to-market loss before any default. Fixed longer notes face duration plus credit-spread repricing; floating loans can have less fixed-rate duration but credit discount and exit-liquidity risk, while higher floating service costs affect issuer cash. In a later restructuring, lower enterprise/pool values, senior dilution, leakage, costs and realization delay reduce distributable proceeds; subordination makes juniors more convex to residual shortfall. A bond's par shortfall is not the investor's entry-price loss: economic loss depends on purchase price, proceeds, interim cash and timing, all of which are missing here. No assumed recovery floor, stress magnitude, PD or portfolio loss is assigned."}],"calculation_id":null,"value_class":"source","source_amount":null,"stated_amount":null,"calculation_status":null,"formula":null,"limitation":null,"display":"Economic loss versus legal loss: spread widening or rates rising can create mark-to-market loss before any default. Fixed longer notes face duration plus credit-spread repricing; floating loans can have less fixed-rate duration but credit discount and exit-liquidity risk, while higher floating service costs affect issuer cash. In a later restructuring, lower enterprise/pool values, senior dilution, leakage, costs and realization delay reduce distributable proceeds; subordination makes juniors more convex to residual shortfall. A bond's par shortfall is not the investor's entry-price loss: economic loss depends on purchase price, proceeds, interim cash and timing, all of which are missing here. No assumed recovery floor, stress magnitude, PD or portfolio loss is assigned.","table_display":"Economic loss versus legal loss: spread widening or rates rising can create mark-to-market loss before any default. Fixed longer notes face duration plus credit-spread repricing; floating loans can have less fixed-rate duration but credit discount and exit-liquidity risk, while higher floating service costs affect issuer cash. In a later restructuring, lower enterprise/pool values, senior dilution, leakage, costs and realization delay reduce distributable proceeds; subordination makes juniors more convex to residual shortfall. A bond's par shortfall is not the investor's entry-price loss: economic loss depends on purchase price, proceeds, interim cash and timing, all of which are missing here. No assumed recovery floor, stress magnitude, PD or portfolio loss is assigned."},{"fact_id":"prose-CP-3-10.r2.c0","label":"Downside