ula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 86","text":"| X03 Acquisition strategy / valuation | Management Language | S1 p.4: \u201cselective acquisition strategy, concentrating on proprietary commercial aerospace component businesses with significant aftermarket content\u201d; p.119 says purchase prices reflect current and expected EBITDA As Defined/cash flows. | Attractive niche claims are hypotheses to test; forward cash expectations in purchase accounting can fail \u2192 no automatic synergy or return credit and no impairment-to-recovery inference. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 87","text":"| X04 September financing/distribution | Documentary Fact | September 19, 2024 issuance of 2033 secured notes and Tranche L; parties in S1 p.131 include TransDigm Inc. issuer, TD Group and subsidiaries guarantors. CP-1 D11/F04 retained below. Same page: proceeds of both issuances plus cash fund special-dividend declaration. BF01 records the action. | Borrowing funded equity cash return without an acquired earnings stream \u2192 debt service rises relative to retention/deleveraging; October settlement limits interpretation of base-date cash. Funding allocation not reconstructed beyond the stated link. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 88","text":"| X05 Declared / paid distributions and repurchases | Documentary Fact | CP-1 IS21, EQ23, CF28/CF29 and BS14 have different scopes. S1 p.146 dates November 2023 declaration/payment and September 2024 declaration, with October 2024 payment separately disclosed. S1 p.140: \u201cNo repurchases were made ... in fiscal 2024 or 2023\u201d; FY2022 repurchases documented. | Recurring use of special distributions and historical buybacks evidences cash-return willingness; no FY2024 buyback is contrary evidence to assuming every authorized return was executed \u2192 track actual cash and obligations, not authorization as payment. No funding source specifically established here for FY2022 buybacks or November common dividend. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 89","text":"| X06 Refinancings / liquidity facilities | Documentary Fact | February 27, 2024 revolver refinancing extended tenor and increased commitments; February notes replaced 2026 notes redeemed March 28. March 22 repricing/Tranche K replaced H; April 22 subordinated-note redemption funded by additional secured notes plus cash; June 4 Amendment 16 extended/repriced loans; July 12 securitization capacity/tenor amendment. S1 pp.128\u2013130. | Tenor extensions and pricing amendments can mitigate historical near-term funding burdens, but do not repay consolidated debt or guarantee repeat access; substituting secured for subordinated claims changes priority mix \u2192 evaluate instrument-specific terms; no coercive LME classification. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 90","text":"| X07 Disposals / rating / regulatory chronology | Insufficient Information | CP-1 CF09 reports gains on sale, not a named completed-disposal chronology; business-risk passages establish regulation but not dated enforcement events. No dated rating record supplied. | Missing event identifiers prevent transaction-specific proceeds/earnings or rating migration conclusions \u2192 retain gains as accounting rows only, and request dated event evidence if needed. No claim that no disposals, downgrades or regulatory events occurred. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 92","text":"### Timeline and governance behavior (absorbed CP-2C)","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"dat