tificial FY2024 closing. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 103","text":"| TL04 | November 2023; November 28, 2023 financing | Documentary Fact | S1 p.146 dates common special dividend paid in November; pp.127\u2013128 notes and J loans for CPI funding. | Distinct contemporaneous actions; do not assign those acquisition proceeds to the November dividend without evidence. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 104","text":"| TL05 | February 27 through April 22, 2024 | Documentary Fact | S1 pp.128\u2013130 revolver/notes refinancing, March 1 FPT acquisition (p.118), March repricing, March 28/April 22 redemptions. | Reduced some historical earlier maturities while modifying claims' secured/subordinated composition. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 105","text":"| TL06 | May 21, June 4, June 6, 2024 | Documentary Fact | S1 pp.117, 130, 115: SEI, Amendment 16, CPI closing respectively. | Acquisition spend plus refinancing execution must be assessed separately from debt reduction. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 106","text":"| TL07 | July 12 and July 31, 2024 | Documentary Fact | S1 p.130 securitization amendment; pp.114\u2013115 Raptor closing. | Additional receivable-backed funding capability and acquisition integration burden; not unrestricted liquidity. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 107","text":"| TL08 | September 19, 2024 financing; September declaration | Documentary Fact | S1 pp.131/146, BF01; purchase-agreement chronology conflict C01 retained below. | Direct evidence of debt-funded extraction; declaration and cash payment are not the same period. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 108","text":"| TL09 | September 30, 2024 base | Documentary Fact | CP-1 BS01, BS14 and D/F registers; S1 p.132 issuer states note covenant compliance. | Cash, declared obligations and accounting debt coexist; issuer compliance statement is not an independent headroom test. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 109","text":"| TL10 | October 2024 \u2014 Subsequent event | Documentary Fact | S1 p.131 remaining securitization draw, CP-1 SE02; p.146 special dividend/equivalents paid, CP-1 SE03. | Post-base funding/outflows, not FY2024 cash flows; no complete post-event cash balance or current liquidity inferred. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 110","text":"| TL11 | November 7, 2024 \u2014 source opinion date | Documentary Fact | S1 pp.58, 104 EY signature dates. | Later assurance about historical reporting, not an operating event at the base date or current credit update. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 112","text":"#### T2D.3 \u2014 governance topics and exact scoring inputs","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 114","text":"The following topic inputs were submitted to `score_governance`. For **every GT topic**, `behaviour_type`, `amount_funding_source` and `legal_capacity_link` were actual JSON nulls in the call; this table displays their treatment as Not applicable \u2014 topic fields. Extraction-Oriented was used only for BF01, not for a topic. Dimension is the topic label after the ID. All GT evidence-quality/category/direction inputs and their limitations are retained here; mechanics and implications are retained in the next table. All citations refer to the full dated sources in Sources.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 116","text":"| ID / dimension | Documented fact supplied to scorer | Direction; evidence quality; category | Citations supplied / limitation |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 117","text":"|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 118","text":"| GT01 Leverage tolerance | September 19, 2024 notes and Tranche L proceeds plus cash funded the special-dividend declaration. | Creditor-Adverse; High; Documentary Fact | S1 Note 10 p.131: \u201cThe proceeds from both fourth quarter of fiscal 2024 issuances were used, along with existing cash on hand, to fund a $75.00 special dividend declaration\u201d. No inference of future target leverage or current willingness. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 119","text":"| GT02 Shareholder extraction risk | Board declared common special dividends during FY2024; the September declaration remained accrued at year end. | Creditor-Adverse; High; Documentary Fact | S1 Note 16 p.146: \u201cThe special dividends totaled $6,153 million, of which $1,937 million was paid in the first quarter of fiscal 2024 and the remaining $4,216 million is accrued as of September 30, 2024.\u201d Declaration is not FY2024 cash settlement; October payments are subsequent events. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 120","text":"| GT03 Acquisition appetite | Repeated acquisitions of Raptor Scientific, CPI Electron Device Business, SEI and FPT in FY2024 follow Calspan in FY2023; CPI financing included debt proceeds. | Mixed; High; Analyst Interpretation | S1 Note 2 p.115: \u201cThe acquisition was financed through existing cash on hand, inclusive of a portion of the cash proceeds from the new long-term debt issued during the first quarter of fiscal 2024\u201d; p.119: \u201cThe fiscal 2024 acquisitions of Raptor Scientific, CPI\u2019s Electron Device Business, SEI and FPT and fiscal 2023 acquisition of Calspan\u201d. No independently tested returns or realized synergies; no numerical future appetite inferred. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 121","text":"| GT04 Support behavior | No sponsor equity injection or binding liquidity-support commitment is established by the supplied evidence. | Insufficient Information; Insufficient; Insufficient Information | No supporting action citation supplied. Sponsor identity, commitment, funding resources and executed support terms Not supplied. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 122","text":"| GT05 Disclosure transparency | Annual report explicitly labels EBITDA As Defined non-GAAP and provides segment and consolidated bridges. | Supportive; High; Documentary Fact | S1 Note 15 pp.141\u2013142: \u201cEBITDA As Defined is not a measurement of financial performance under U.S. GAAP.\u201d Limited to supplied annual disclosure; proxy availability is not scored. CP-1 bridge-scope residuals remain unresolved; its alleged maturity conflict is withdrawn as a host/model calendar-fiscal error (C02). |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 123","text":"| GT06 Creditor treatment / amendment behavior | Amendment 16 repriced and extended loans; the subordinated-note redemption was financed with secured notes and cash. | Mixed; High; Analyst Interpretation | S1 Note 10 p.130: \u201cusing the net proceeds of the offering of the $550 million 2029 Secured Notes, together with cash on hand.\u201d Same page: \u201camended and extended $2,644 million of existing Tranche I term loans maturing August 24, 2028 and converting such loans into Tranche J term loans maturing February 28, 2031.\u201d No priming, non-pro-rata exchange or coercion established; other operative facilities are not supplied. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 124","text":"| GT07 Legal-capacity linkage | Executed 2033 indenture contains conditional restricted-payment permissions; actual elections and compliance calculations are not supplied. | Insufficient Information; Insufficient; Insufficient Information | L tool p.18 \u00a74.07 L1265: \u201cthe Company and its Restricted Subsidiaries may make any Restricted Payment so long as (1) no Default or Event of Default has occurred and is continuing\u201d. Definitions, complete package, election/use ledger and certificates required; provision also imposes a pro forma fixed-charge coverage condition. No legal behavior score supported. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 125","text":"| GT08 Reporting quality | EY reports fair presentation under GAAP and effective internal controls, with acquired-business controls excluded from ICFR scope. | Supportive; High; Documentary Fact | S1 EY November 7, 2024 reports p.103: \u201cthe consolidated financial statements present fairly, in all material respects\u201d; p.57: \u201cOur audit of internal control over financial reporting of the Company also did not include an evaluation of the internal control over financial reporting of Raptor Scientific, CPI\u2019s Electron Device Business, SEI or FPT.\u201d Audit is not independent assurance by this module; no visual fidelity review; CP-1 source conflicts not resolved. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 126","text":"| GT09 Related-party leakage risk | Annual report incorporates related transactions and director independence information from an unavailable proxy. | Insufficient Information; Insufficient; Insufficient Information | S1 Item 13 p.61: \u201cThe information required by this item will be set forth under the captions entitled \u2018Corporate Governance\u2019 and \u2018Director Compensation\u2019 in our Proxy Statement, which is incorporated herein by reference.\u201d Proxy, related-party contracts and fee schedules Not supplied. Source boundary is not adverse disclosure behavior. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 128","text":"| Scoring input ID | Risk mechanic supplied | Credit implication supplied |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 129","text":"|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 130","text":"| GT01 | New borrowing funds a non-earning distribution rather than debt retirement, increasing fixed claims without an acquired earnings stream. | Greater debt-service burden and lower deleveraging priority in this historical event. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 131","text":"| GT02 | A declared cash obligation competes with debt service and makes base-date cash an incomplete indicator of retained liquidity. | Monitor subsequent settlement and future distributions; do not regard the year-end cash balance as permanently surplus. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 132","text":"| GT03 | Acquisitions add product exposures and earnings opportunities but consume cash and, for CPI, borrowing, while preliminary allocations and integration create execution uncertainty. | Test post-acquisition cash contribution and leverage rather than assume synergies or full-year earnings. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 133","text":"| GT04 | There is no evidenced external support to incorporate into a liquidity or refinancing case. | Underwrite without assumed sponsor support, not as a conclusion that support would be refused. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 134","text":"| GT05 | Explicit definition boundaries and a bridge allow creditors to distinguish adjusted performance from GAAP earnings. | Supports bounded historical analytical traceability, not automatic add-back acceptance. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 135","text":"| GT06 | Extensions reduce nearer contractual refinancing needs, but substituting secured borrowing for subordinated debt can change the priority mix for remaining creditors. | Evaluate instrument-specific ranking and refinancing burdens; these actions do not establish a coercive LME. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 136","text":"| GT07 | A conditional contractual permission cannot identify unused capacity or the route actually relied on for a distribution. | No quantified headroom or compliance certification; route to legal review. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 137","text":"| GT08 | Audited statements support historical reliability while the acquisition exclusion limits the reach of controls assurance. | Use audited financials with explicit scope limits and monitor integration and unresolved cross-presentation items. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 138","text":"| GT09 | Without the proxy, affiliate relationships and any fees cannot be assessed; disclosed option dividends alone do not prove improper leakage. | Request related-party evidence before any leakage or alignment conclusion. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 140","text":"#### T2D.4 \u2014 behavior flags and support/extraction distinction","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 142","text":"These are the two actual behavior-flag rows supplied to the scoring call. Both carry High evidence quality and Documentary Fact category. GT rows and BF rows overlap evidence and are not additive transaction counts.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 144","text":"| Field | BF01 September 2024 debt-funded special dividend | BF02 June 2024 loan amendment |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 145","text":"|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 146","text":"| Documented fact | September 19, 2024 secured notes and Tranche L were used with existing cash to fund the special-dividend declaration; cash paid in October. | Amendment 16 lowered Tranche J spread and extended part of Tranche I into Tranche J. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 147","text":"| Direction / behaviour_type / dimension | Extraction-Oriented / dividend recap / Shareholder extraction risk | Mixed / amendment / Creditor treatment / amendment behavior |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 148","text":"| amount_funding_source | USD millions: notes principal 1,500 and Tranche L principal 1,500, plus existing cash; common dividend 75 USD/share; October common payment 4,216 and equivalents 132. Not all proceeds allocated dollar-for-dollar by the report. | USD millions: 997 existing J repriced; 2,644 existing I amended and extended; no sponsor contribution evidenced. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 149","text":"| legal_capacity_link | Capacity: section 4.07 contains conditional permissions, not a quantified certificate; actual basket election unavailable. Willingness: declaration and funding link documented. Feasibility: historical issuance and later payments documented, not current accessible liquidity or market access. | Capacity: annual summary does not supply operative voting/consent terms. Willingness: amendment executed as reported. Feasibility: historical extension achieved, not proof of future refinancing access. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 150","text":"| risk_mechanic | Debt-funded transfer to equity leaves fixed claims but no corresponding operating asset; accrued payment makes cash timing material. | Extends contractual funding tenor and lowers spread, while debt remains outstanding and transaction costs arise. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 151","text":"| credit_implication | Raises extraction monitoring priority and restricts mechanical year-end cash-netted leverage interpretation. | Historical refinancing mitigation, not deleveraging or creditor support; evaluate remaining maturities separately. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 152","text":"| Citations / quotes | S1 Note 10 p.131: \u201cThe proceeds from both fourth quarter of fiscal 2024 issuances were used, along with existing cash on hand, to fund a $75.00 special dividend declaration\u201d; Note 16 p.146: \u201cThe Company paid $4,216 million and $132 million in special dividend and dividend equivalents, respectively, in October 2024.\u201d | S1 Note 10 p.130, June 4, 2024 Amendment 16: \u201crepriced all of its $997 million in existing Tranche J term loans to bear interest at Term SOFR plus 2.50% compared to Term SOFR plus 3.25% applicable prior to Amendment No. 16\u201d |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 153","text":"| limitation | October payment is subsequent to September 30, 2024; not current underwriting. No certification of legal compliance. | No amendment vote records or current facility status supplied. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 155","text":"No Supportive support flag was manufactured. Shareholder extraction is not itself proof of priming, unlawful leakage or a coercive liability-management exercise. No supplied action establishes an equity rescue or a refusal to support. Cash from option exercises (CP-1 CF27) is not an emergency sponsor injection. Historical debt issuance feasibility cannot certify future access.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 157","text":"#### T2D.5\u2013T2D.8 \u2014 capacity, capital allocation, disclosure and contrary evidence","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 159","text":"**Capacity versus willingness versus feasibility.** L tool pp.16\u201318 \u00a74.07 L1202\u2013L1277 defines restricted payments and conditions/exceptions; L1265 includes both no continuing default and a pro forma Consolidated Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio exceeding 2.0 to 1.0. L1272\u2013L1274 contains continuing-obligation and classification/combination provisions. These are operative words requiring complete definitions and fact inputs, not a calculation using CP-1 K11. L tool p.16 \u00a74.04 L1185\u2013L1188 requires officers' compliance certificates; none is supplied. S1 p.132 states issuer covenant compliance; it is management's documentary assertion, not this module's compliance opinion. Willingness is demonstrated by BF01, not by the existence of \u00a74.07. Feasibility is limited to historical issuance/payment actions; cash accessibility, remaining baskets and current market access remain unestablished. No statement that the September distribution relied on a particular basket is made.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 161","text":"**Capital allocation.** X01\u2013X06 and CP-1 financial rows show acquisitions and shareholder returns alongside refinancing. Asset purchases may add earnings but need integration and contribution testing; distributions remove resources without adding operating earnings. S1 pp.115\u2013120 records open measurement periods for FY2024 acquisitions, with pro forma results described as not material and not provided. This is not evidence of no earnings contribution or no integration risk. No forward earnings or synergy estimate is filled in. A named disposal register is unavailable despite CF09 sale gains; no proceeds use is invented.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 163","text":"**Disclosure and controls.** GT05/GT08 provide supportive evidence from actual reconciliations and audited reporting, not from a proxy-incorporation sentence. S1 pp.56\u201357 excludes acquired-company controls from the ICFR scope while retaining those companies in consolidated financial statements. S1 p.104 identifies goodwill valuation as a critical audit matter, with sensitivity to discount rates, growth and EBITDA margins; this is estimation sensitivity, not an adverse audit opinion. CP-1 C03\u2013C05 below qualify particular definition uses; C02 records withdrawal of the host/model maturity error, not an issuer inconsistency. No broad poor-disclosure conclusion or score is drawn from missing proxy material.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 165","text":"**Contrary evidence.** No FY2024/FY2023 buybacks under the program (S1 p.140); audited reporting and explicit non-GAAP caution (pp.103, 141); historical maturity extensions and spread reductions (pp.128\u2013130); multiple product/customer/end-market exposures (pp.5\u20137). These temper a one-sided extraction narrative but do not reverse BF01's cash/debt mechanics. Conversely, government contract rights, OEM cyclicality, supplier requalification constraints and channel-mix sensitivity counter an unconditional aftermarket-resilience thesis. Supportive reporting does not offset an actual cash distribution, and absent support evidence is neither neutral nor adverse.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 167","text":"#### Conflicts register \u2014 retained issues and withdrawn host/model error","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 169","text":"| ID | Conflicting spans / exact source roles | Treatment and credit impact |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 170","text":"|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 171","text":"| C01 Purchase-agreement date | S1 Note 10 p.131: \u201cOn September 19, 2024, the Company entered into a purchase agreement\u201d; L tool p.32 Appendix L2482: \u201cthe Purchase Agreement dated September 5, 2024\u201d; L2481 Issue Date September 19, 2024. | Preserve narrative agreement date and defined agreement date separately. No reconciliation, preferred date or inferred explanation. Exact agreement needed if chronology affects a legal conclusion. Neither conflict creates a current transaction. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 172","text":"| C02 Withdrawn host/model calendar-fiscal error; corrected CP-1 G13 | S1 p.43: \u201cThere is no maturity on any tranche of term loans or notes until November 2027 (fiscal 2028).\u201d S1 p.46 reports 5.50% notes principal 2,650 due November 15, 2027; p.133 reports fiscal 2027 repayment 92. | November 15, 2027 falls in fiscal 2028, not fiscal 2027. The alleged conflict is withdrawn, not an issuer inconsistency or unresolved maturity gap. Preserve all reported fiscal buckets without reallocating amounts. A complete instrument/amortization allocation is not established by this mapping; no issuer reconciliation is requested solely for the withdrawn error. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 173","text":"| C03 Lease wording, inherited CP-1 T4.11 | S1 p.131 describes minimum payments \u201cnet of the current portion\u201d as 262/193; CP-1 LS15\u2013LS17, S1 p.148 explicitly show current 6/5, long-term 256/188, total 262/193. | Retain wording conflict; no new reconciliation. CP-1 retains explicit Note 17 accounting classifications; this module makes no competing choice. Prevent duplicate current-lease additions or legal indebtedness inference. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 174","text":"| C04 Cash-block scope, inherited CP-1 R28 | S1 p.54 reported bridge changes 272/415 versus CP-1 K03 absolute complete cash-flow block 302/431, S1 p.109; residuals 30/16. | Distinct reported/derived definitions, not forced equal; not proof of misconduct. Adjustment-to-cash interpretation needs definition alignment. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 175","text":"| C05 Dividend scope, inherited CP-1 R29 | S1 p.108/CP-1 EQ23 equity charge magnitude 6,368 versus Note 16 p.146 common declared 6,153 and vested equivalents 233; CP-1 comparison residual (18). | Scope equivalence not established. Preserve each field and CP-1 residual; do not change paid or declared amounts to force alignment. Not an assertion statements fail to balance. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 177","text":"#### T2D.9\u2013T2D.11 \u2014 credit translations, monitoring and handoff boundaries","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 179","text":"| ID | Category | Evidence \u2192 risk mechanic \u2192 credit implication | Contrary evidence / unresolved conflict |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 180","text":"|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 181","text":"| CT01 Revenue durability | Analyst Interpretation | B03/B04, S1 p.4 aftermarket estimate and historical characterization, plus B10 demand drivers \u2192 long-lived installed equipment supports repeat consumption, conditional on utilization and mix \u2192 business-risk mitigant for historical synthesis, not contracted debt-service coverage or a guaranteed forecast. | B10/B14 cyclicality, 