les, board/certificate records and actual upstream cash constraints; no independent-director approval requirement inferred |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 81","text":"| F10 Guarantees/entity reach \u2014 \u00a7\u00a74.17,10.01\u201310.08; L pp.20,27\u201328 | Senior payment guarantee if restricted sub is facility borrower/guarantor **or** issues/guarantees Capital Markets Indebtedness of Company/Guarantor **at least 200**; deliver within **20 Business Days** | 200 threshold belongs to capital-markets limb, not both limbs; definition excludes these Notes/Additional Notes, facilities and specified other debt; release and fraudulent-transfer limits remain | Holdings and executed subsidiary guarantors; signing UK entity expressly present | Post-issue accessions, facility borrower/guarantor map, guarantee triggers/dates, solvency and full subsidiary assets/earnings |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 82","text":"| F11 Collateral/perfection/release/ICA \u2014 \u00a7\u00a74.20,11.16,12.01\u201312.08; L pp.21,29\u201331 | Impairment restriction for material collateral; further assurance/joinder and after-acquired requirements; initial perfection efforts within 90 days if not perfected at issue | Excluded Collateral defined in absent Security Agreement; after-acquired coverage conditions track other secured debt/facilities; releases for permitted transfers, guarantee release and specified bank lien release | Grantors' defined collateral, not all consolidated assets; ICA expressly controls | Security documents, exclusion schedules, mortgages, IP/UCC/local filings, actual completion and ICA enforcement provisions |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 83","text":"| F12 Change of control/redemption \u2014 \u00a7\u00a71.01,3.07\u20133.08,4.15; L pp.4,15,20 | Conditional holder offer at **101% plus accrued interest**; defined >50% voting control, all/substantially all transfers or specified liquidation | Notice within 30 days; purchase 30\u201360 days after notice; prior facility/specified senior debt repayment or consent; third-party compliant offer or prior redemption-notice exceptions; advanced offer may be conditional | Notes tendered, not an automatic funded redemption of all debt; no scheduled sinking fund | Control transaction facts, other debt consent/repayment, tenders, cash funding and exact authenticated maturity date |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 84","text":"| F13 Defaults/remedies \u2014 \u00a7\u00a76.01\u20136.10,7.01; L pp.22\u201324 | 30-day interest grace; principal due default without equivalent grace; other-covenant 60 days after notice, reporting 180; cross-final-maturity/acceleration >=50; final judgments >50 unstayed/unpaid 60 days | 25% acceleration; Company insolvency automatic; facility amounts outstanding invoke earlier of facility acceleration or five Business Days after specified notice, if EoD continues; collateral-failure test >50 with specified 60-day limb | Company/Significant Subsidiaries for relevant defaults; securitization entity excluded from cross-debt limb | Actual defaults/notices, debt status, judgments, valuations and full ICA controls; no bespoke EBITDA equity-cure mechanic identified in supplied indenture |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 85","text":"| F14 Amendments/suspension/defeasance \u2014 Articles VIII\u2013IX, \u00a7\u00a72.09,4.19; L pp.14,20\u201321,25\u201327 | General majority; affected-holder sacred rights; **66\u2154%** for nonpermitted all/substantially all collateral release or materially adverse ICA modification; IG/no-default suspension | No-consent amendments enumerated; permitted releases not caught by nonpermitted release threshold; dual-IG suspension does not suspend \u00a74.12 or \u00a74.15; funded defeasance has independent conditions | Single notes class including Additional Notes; Company/control-affiliate notes excluded from votes subject to trustee knowledge protection | Voting register, full ICA consent overlays, ratings/notices, actual supplements, trust funding and opinions; no assumption suspension or defeasance occurred |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 87","text":"### Legal risks and protections","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 89","text":"**Definitions change capacity, not just reported leverage.** L p.5 L410\u2013L424 defines FCCR as legal EBITDA over Fixed Charges for four full quarters with internal statements, pro forma financing and acquisitions/dispositions, transaction-date floating rates and swap effects. Fixed Charges adds tax-grossed preferred dividends to defined interest. Defined interest excludes financing-fee amortization, bridge/commitment fees, qualified securitization costs and prepayment premiums, while adding capitalized interest and capital-lease interest. EBITDA includes expansive transaction, restructuring, dividend-equivalent and projected-savings adjustments. Clause M's 35% limit is neither a global cap on all EBITDA add-backs nor a cap on every pro forma acquisition adjustment: L421\u2013L422 separately permits officer-good-faith acquisition calculations and reasonably determined operating expense reductions. The no-duplication and specified exclusions still matter; the document is not permission to add the same amount twice. Wider earnings and narrower fixed charges can make ratio debt and distributions easier before actual cash savings arrive, increasing debt-service sensitivity and weakening the residual asset cushion. Monitor adjustment categories, actual realization and transaction-date rate inputs, not the accounting multiple.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 91","text":"**Debt and lien permissions are separate.** L p.18 \u00a74.09 L1295 says **\u201cgreater than 2.0 to 1.0\u201d**, not greater than or equal. L p.10 L715 says **\u201cshall not exceed 5.25 to 1.00\u201d** for the specific (xxxi) Ratio Indebtedness lien route. Permitted Liens (iii) covers Bank Indebtedness; (xx) links purchase-money and additional-debt baskets to asset-specific/collateral-only limits; (xxi) confines foreign-sub liens to foreign-sub assets. Accordingly, 5.25 is not a blanket secured leverage maintenance ceiling or a condition on every lien. Permitted-debt reclassification can refresh fixed baskets; acquisition debt can use an improved-FCCR alternative even without satisfying the USD1 ratio-debt test. These provisions can permit further pari claims or locally senior funding without a new breach, but actual priming is not established. The contrary case is \u00a74.12's express junior-or-permitted requirement and \u00a79.02's affected-holder ranking protection. A proposed priority change must satisfy those boundaries and the missing ICA, rather than relying on a generic majority-vote claim.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 93","text":"**Leakage can occur before default and may outlast deteriorating tests.** \u00a74.07 L1265 permits **\u201cany Restricted Payment\u201d** subject to no continuing Default/EoD and pro forma FCCR exceeding 2.0x. L1272 preserves certain payments contractually committed while conditions held. The builder basket therefore is not the sole potential distribution constraint. Permitted Investments can reach non-guarantors, and designation of a guarantor as Unrestricted can release its guarantee and liens under \u00a7\u00a710.07(c),12.07(f), subject to designation and RP conditions. Asset-sale exclusions, \u00a75.01's intragroup carveout and affiliate carveouts mean a transfer may avoid one covenant yet remain subject to others. No categorical IP-transfer prohibition is identified in the supplied indenture; this is a conditional route, not a finding that material IP has been transferred. Without an entity/IP schedule, valuation and usage ledger its amount is Not calculable. These mechanics can reduce creditors' reachable value without an immediate payment default; monitor designations, intragroup transfers, RP commitments and releases as well as reported dividends.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 95","text":"**The historical distribution demonstrates willingness, not a capacity opinion.** S1 p.131 expressly links September notes and Tranche L proceeds plus existing cash to the USD75/share declaration and eligible option equivalents. S1 p.146 records USD4,216 million common dividends accrued at September 30 and USD4,216 million common plus USD132 million equivalent payments in **October 2024**. The latter are subsequent cash uses, not FY2024 cash flow. Neither the funding link nor the issuer compliance statement on p.132 identifies the precise \u00a74.07 route, verifies conditions at declaration/commitment or proves residual capacity. A general compliance assertion is not the missing transaction certificate. Retain CP-1A BF01 as extraction behavior, not unlawful payment or coercive LME evidence.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 97","text":"**Asset-sale protection is real but delayed and qualified.** FMV consideration and conditional cash requirements, reinvestment/application deadlines, and a pro rata 100%-plus-interest offer protect noteholders where \u00a74.10 applies. Countervailing flexibility includes deemed cash (assumed liabilities, instruments converted within 180 days and designated noncash consideration), long reinvestment periods, net-proceeds deductions, use to repay secured or non-guarantor debt, and return of untendered residual to permitted general purposes. The special productive-assets alternative requires substitute Productive Assets promptly to become Collateral where sold assets were collateral (L1317). This supports collateral continuity in that path, but is not a universal requirement that all proceeds immediately repay these Notes. Do not collapse asset-sales proceeds into near-term note amortization.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 99","text":"**Guarantees improve direct recourse but are neither universal nor permanent.** \u00a710.01 promises unconditional, irrevocable, joint-and-several payment/performance, not merely collection, with reinstatement for rescinded payments; \u00a710.02 limits enforceability by fraudulent-transfer law. The executed signer list includes CPI, Calspan, Raptor entities and TransDigm UK, among others (L pp.31\u201332), but is not a current exhaustive ownership/value schedule. \u00a74.17's facility limb and separate >=200 capital-markets limb can capture new obligors, with 20-Business-Day accession; \u00a712.04 links required guarantee accession to security/ICA joinder. \u00a710.07 nonetheless releases on permitted external disposals, compliant USub designation, immateriality under its conditions, release from specified triggering debt, or funded discharge/defeasance. Immaterial Domestic Restricted Subsidiary requires both \u003c=2.5% EBITDA and \u003c=2.5% assets, using the specified >45-day reporting lag (L p.7 L535); no aggregate immateriality cap is stated in that definition. A non-guarantor is not the same as an Unrestricted Subsidiary, and a foreign subsidiary is not automatically outside every guarantee: TransDigm UK is expressly excluded from the defined Foreign Restricted Subsidiary category and signs here.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 101","text":"**Security documentation determines realized control.** Collateral excludes the absent Security Agreement's Excluded Collateral (L p.4 L389). \u00a712.03 conditions some further collateralization on corresponding facility requirements; \u00a712.06 provides commercially reasonable perfection efforts and a 90-day outside period, not evidence those filings were completed. \u00a712.07(e)(B) follows specified Credit Agreement Collateral Agent releases, but excludes the stated full-cash facility discharge outside foreclosure/remedies; it is not an automatic release whenever the facility is repaid. \u00a712.07(e)(A) can release collateral transferred outside Company/Holdings/Guarantors in a permitted transaction, potentially including a restricted non-guarantor recipient, subject to full operative conditions. Permitted automatic releases differ from amendments releasing substantially all collateral outside the documents. Certificates and opinions are required to evidence requested releases; none is supplied here.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 103","text":"**LME/control protection is mixed rather than absent.** \u00a79.02 expressly contemplates consents in tender/exchange offers; general covenant changes can bind dissenters by majority. However, affected-holder protections include principal, fixed maturity, redemption terms, interest/payment timing, currency, payment suit, adversely changed ranking and specified post-trigger change-of-control obligations. L p.27 L1857 protects changes **\u201caffecting the subordination or ranking of the Notes or the Guarantees\u201d** adverse to holders. A materially adverse ICA modification or unauthorized all/substantially all collateral release needs 66\u2154%, not merely majority. \u00a72.09 excludes issuer/control-affiliate votes, with trustee actual-knowledge protection. \u00a76.06 prohibits using the indenture to obtain preference over another holder; \u00a76.07 preserves individual due-payment suits. These are meaningful opposite-case barriers. They do not prove that every non-pro-rata exchange, open-market purchase or asset-based transaction is prohibited, or that a majority can validly override every priority right. No executed coercive LME, uptier or drop-down is established by the supplied actions.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 105","text":"### Analytical appendix \u2014 additional legal registers","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 107","text":"#### Conditional debt, investment and payment permissions \u2014 capacity register","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 109","text":"All amounts below are documentary USD-million parameters, not unused capacity. Current legal inputs, usage and remaining capacity for every row are **Not supplied / Not calculable because no legal reconciliation and election/use ledger is provided**. Permissions may overlap or reclassify; they are not summed. Definitions and operative conditions control over this compressed register.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 111","text":"| Permission / evidence | Formula or operative boundary | Borrower flexibility / creditor limit | Retest or missing use evidence |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 112","text":"|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_t