operty/commitments, ordinary-course purpose, legal earnings and security terms |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 124","text":"| Deemed cash/asset sale, L pp.18\u201319 | Noncash basket greater of 150 or 5% Total Assets outstanding; 545-day application, binding commitment plus 120 days; 180-day prior investment credit; 40 offer aggregation | Asset monetization can avoid immediate cash repayment while retaining reinvestment option | Designations, valuations, proceeds conversion and application calendar |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 126","text":"#### Legal entity / guarantee / security reach register","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 128","text":"| Entity or location | Role and reach | Boundary / release and value mechanic | Evidence and confidence |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 129","text":"|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 130","text":"| TransDigm Inc. | Delaware operating issuer; direct payment claim and Grantor | Direct recourse to its assets subject to liens/exclusions; its consolidated assets are not all owned directly | L p.1 L225; p.7 L525; \u00a7\u00a710,12. High for role; entity asset value Not supplied |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 131","text":"| TD Group / Holdings | Delaware holding parent; upstream guarantee and Grantor, not the Company | Joint-and-several guarantee; Holdings release expressly addressed on discharge/defeasance; no assumed operating asset value | L pp.1,27\u201328 \u00a7\u00a710.01,10.07(f); CP-1 T4.2. High for role |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 132","text":"| Executed subsidiary guarantors, including UK | Downstream group supports issuer and shares collateral obligations within applicable terms | Examples CPI International/CPI Intermediate/CPI Subsidiary Holdings; Calspan LLC/Holdings; Raptor Labs Holdco/Intermediate; TransDigm UK Holdings Limited; not a complete current ownership schedule | L pp.31\u201332 L2256\u2013L2441; \u00a7\u00a74.17,10.01,12.04. Signature roster read; no jurisdiction inferred from names |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 133","text":"| Restricted non-guarantors | Within several covenant tests, outside direct guarantee until trigger/voluntary accession | Permitted investment recipients and local debt may retain value beyond direct note recourse; USD400 ratio-debt limit not a limit on all non-guarantor debt | L \u00a7\u00a71.01,4.09,4.17. Conditional structural exposure, Medium; amounts Not supplied |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 134","text":"| Unrestricted subsidiaries | Designated group outside restricted covenant perimeter; subsidiaries follow designation | Fair-value RP treatment/certification required; guarantor designation releases guarantee/liens; actions not deemed restricted-group actions | L p.12 L815\u2013L819; p.18 L1275\u2013L1277; \u00a7\u00a710.07,12.07. Route theoretical; no actual designation register supplied |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 135","text":"| TransDigm Receivables LLC | Express Securitization Entity as of issue date; separate receivable-financing pool | Standard non-recourse/undertaking limits and residual interests; no assumed note lien on securitized pool | L p.11 L760\u2013L771; S1 p.130. High for defined designation; actual residual value Not supplied |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 136","text":"| Foreign collateral / IP / excluded assets | UK Debenture Collateral and defined US collateral references, not complete asset descriptions | US trustee/agent does not undertake foreign-law execution; security exclusions/perfection/local enforcement remain gaps | L pp.4,6,11,30\u201331 \u00a7\u00a71.01,12.01(k),12.03. No guaranteed worldwide perfected lien claimed |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 138","text":"#### Intercreditor, enforcement and creditor-control register","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 140","text":"| Control issue | Supported indenture provision | Creditor consequence / contrary protection | ICA-dependent limitation |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 141","text":"|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 142","text":"| Governing control | \u00a7\u00a711.16,12.02,12.08, L pp.29\u201331: ICA controls conflicts and enforcement of guarantees/collateral | Note majority control is not necessarily all-first-lien enforcement control | Full ICA not supplied: applicable representative selection, enforcement votes, override thresholds Not supplied |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 143","text":"| Standstill | \u00a76.02 five-Business-Day/facility-acceleration sequencing; \u00a76.06 60-day trustee-request process | Distinct note acceleration and suit delays; \u00a76.07 individual due-payment suit preserved | Neither period is an ICA standstill. ICA standstill duration, trigger and expiry Not supplied |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 144","text":"| Direct enforcement | \u00a712.01(a), L p.29: holders cannot individually or collectively directly enforce Security Documents; agents act subject to proper directions | Collective control may avoid disorderly seizures; individual holder cannot equate claim ownership with foreclosure power | Actual controlling class/agent and decision mechanism require ICA/security text |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 145","text":"| Turnover / purchase option | No full operative ICA term supplied; Article VI note proceeds priorities do not replace it | Cannot infer no turnover obligation or no buyout rights | Turnover scope, insolvency distributions, purchase-option amount/timing and conditions Not supplied |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 146","text":"| Releases | \u00a7\u00a710.07,12.07; \u00a79.02 protection for nonpermitted substantially-all release | Express releases can remove guarantee and lien reach without fresh holder vote; unauthorized sweeping release has supermajority barrier | ICA release power and class consents Not supplied; requested release evidence needs certificates/opinions |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 147","text":"| Distribution priorities | \u00a76.10 puts trustee/agent costs first, note claims ratably next; \u00a77.07 prior expense lien | Enforcement expenses reduce distributable pool; internal note parity protection exists | Not a complete intercreditor waterfall or recovery estimate |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 148","text":"| Notices and trustee duties | \u00a7\u00a74.03(c),7.01\u20137.05,12.01; L pp.16,23\u201324,29\u201330 | Receipt of financial reports not constructive covenant notice; reliance/indemnity and limited investigative duties can delay creditor response | No assumed agent verification of calculations, filings, value or perfection; obtain evidence rather than rely on agent appointment |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 150","text":"#### Default detail, suspension and funded exit","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 152","text":"Payment/nonpayment and notice conditions must not be conflated. Interest gets 30 days (\u00a76.01(a)); principal and due tender payments do not receive that same grace (\u00a76.01(b)). Other covenants require notice from trustee or 25% holders and 60 days, reporting 180 days; \u00a75.01 requires notice but not that passage of time (\u00a76.01(c)). Cross-debt default is a **final-maturity payment failure or acceleration**, not every debt covenant breach; threshold is at least USD50 million and excludes Securitization Entities in that limb. Final/nonappealable judgments use **in excess of** USD50 million and a 60-day unpaid/unstayed test. Collateral failure above USD50 million has a 60-day persistence limb, while a court pleading repudiating validity is separately covered (\u00a76.01(h)). The Company or Significant Subsidiary insolvency events are covered, but automatic acceleration under the controlling \u00a76.02 applies to **Company** bankruptcy events; others use the stated declaration mechanism. Majority can rescind acceleration under conditions and waive nonpayment-excepted past defaults; it cannot simply waive continuing ordinary payment defaults for all dissenters (\u00a7\u00a76.02,6.04,6.07).","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 154","text":"\u00a74.19 requires both agencies' investment-grade ratings and no continuing Default for suspension. Suspended provisions include RP, upstream restrictions, incurrence, asset sales, affiliates, business, guarantees, preferred stock, impairment and specified merger ratio condition; **liens and change-of-control remain outside that list**. Reversion is prospective, with suspension-period debt allocated under its specified treatment, no retroactive breach solely for suspension-period acts and a 30-day catch-up guarantee accession. Actual suspension notices/ratings are Not supplied; no conclusion that covenants were switched off is made.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 156","text":"Article VIII defeasance is different from ratings suspension: irrevocable USD cash/noncallable government-securities funding sufficient in independent accountants' opinion, tax/legal opinions, officers' certificates, no-default and specified 91-day bankruptcy conditions are required. Covenant defeasance releases the listed covenants including lien/change-of-control obligations and specified cross-default/judgment events; legal defeasance discharges broader obligations with surviving trust-payment rights. Discharge under \u00a78.06 has its own cancellation/due-within-one-year funding conditions. These are not unfunded unilateral covenant escapes, and no exercise is evidenced.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 158","text":"#### PD / LGD / monitoring and opposite-case register","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 160","text":"PD and LGD are qualitative transmission channels, not estimated probabilities or recovery percentages. All rows are Analyst Interpretation grounded in the referenced documentary provisions.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 162","text":"| Priority / provision | Risk mechanic and PD channel | LGD / security-selection channel | Contrary case and observable trigger |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 163","text":"|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 164","text":"| 1 \u2014 \u00a7\u00a74.07,1.01 legal earnings | Ratio-based distributions and commitment grandfathering may preserve cash extraction despite later weaker performance; reduces retained servicing flexibility | Cash exits without acquired operating assets; no recovery value assigned | No-default and strict >2 coverage, exclusions and corporate-law limits still apply. Obtain transaction certificate and monitor new declarations, legal adjustment growth and cash settlement |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 165","text":"| 2 \u2014 \u00a7\u00a74.09,4.12 / Permitted Liens | Separate debt and lien permissions may fund acquisitions/refinancing or releveraging without maintenance breach | Pari dilution and local non-guarantor security can reduce residual value for existing claims | Junior-or-permitted lien requirement, specific 5.25 route and ranking sacred right constrain overt rewrite. Trigger: new debt classifications, collateral grants, LCA signing or exchange terms |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 166","text":"| 3 \u2014 Permitted Investments / \u00a7\u00a710.07,12.07 | Intragroup/USub flexibility may sustain operations or fund assets away from note obligors | Guarantee and lien releases can strand value; structural priority differs from payment ranking | FMV RP designation treatment, no-recourse conditions, guarantee accession and other-package covenants may block route. Trigger: designation certificates, IP/asset transfers, bank lien release or guarantee exit |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 167","text":"| 4 \u2014 \u00a7\u00a74.10,3.09 | Reinvestment/prepayment options support business continuity but delay mandatory note offers | Collateral substitution, repayment of other permitted debt and net deductions change pool | FMV, conditional cash consideration, required collateral substitution in productive-asset route and offer discipline can protect value. Trigger: sale closing, proceeds conversion, 545-day/extension calendar and 40 aggregation |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 168","text":"| 5 \u2014 Articles VI/IX/XII | Notice/grace/collective control can postpone acceleration and workout response; majority amendment may ease default pressure | Agent-led security enforcement and missing ICA affect timing, costs and class bargaining | Individual payment rights, 25% acceleration and affected-holder/66\u2154% barriers constrain majority action. Trigger: formal defaults, consent solicitations, ICA changes and collateral challenges |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 170","text":"**Time-aware downside:** an aerospace utilization/supply shock in CP-2 first reduces deliverable shipments or mix, then cash collection and legal earnings. There is no automatic numerical notes-maintenance breach solely because EBITDA falls. New incurrence/RP ability may tighten at transaction dates, while previously compliant contractual RP commitments may still drain cash; LCA tests may already have been locked at signing. If refinancing/receivables liquidity becomes insufficient, a missed payment, cross-final-maturity failure or acceleration can engage Article VI after its actual notice/grace rules. Enforcement then moves through agents and the missing ICA, with permitted releases and competing liens determining reachable value. Observable triggers are transaction certificates, commitment dates, liquidity events, formal notices, collateral releases and agent directions\u2014not an invented covenant breach date or forecast.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 172","text":"The strongest creditor-friendly case would win if complete documents and certificates showed ample tested coverage using realized cash earnings, restricted unused leakage, retained collateral/guarantor value and enforceable collective controls. Historical business resilience, successful tenor extensions and reporting transparency in CP-1A/CP-2 support that possibility, but do not establish those legal facts. Conversely, broad permissions alone do not establish an actual adverse LME. This distinction reduces confidence in implementation, not confidence that the quoted conditions exist.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 174","text":"#### Aggressiveness rubric and comparison boundary","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 176","text":"| Area | Score 1\u20135 | Evidence / mechanic | Credit implication / confidence |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 177","text":"|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 178","text":"| Notes maintenance architecture | 4 | F01: incurrence rather than periodic ratio maintenance 