ber_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 65","text":"CP-1's retained annual CFO less capex is 1,880/1,236/829 in FY2024/FY2023/FY2022, before acquisitions and distributions. Acquisitions net of cash acquired were cash outflows 2,347/762/437, and dividends/equivalents paid were 2,038/38/1,091 (CF22\u2013CF24/CF28; S1 p.109). Thus E1/E2 support operating capacity, not automatic cash available to retire securities. No acquired full-year earnings, maintenance-capex split or accepted add-back restatement is invented.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 67","text":"### Relative value assessment","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 69","text":"**RV is Unclear for every instrument.** Coupons and contractual SOFR margins are known in the annual source, but neither is an executable yield, OAS, YTW or discount margin. September 2024 issuance at par for the 2033 notes and historical issue discounts elsewhere are transaction facts, not September 30 closing quotes and not November 2026 trading levels. No bid/ask, quote timestamp, accrued interest, dealer depth, traded volume or comparable market curve is supplied. Accordingly, there is no supported cheap/fair/rich label, peer spread differential or spread-based preference.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 71","text":"The conditional comparison is still substantive. All identified debt is USD reported, but fixed notes and floating loans have different rate risk, reset conventions, maturity and optionality. I/K carry SOFR plus 2.75%; J/L plus 2.50% in the base-date annual terms. That does not prove I/K offer better return: different prices, tenor, amortization, repricing rights and loan documents can offset the margin difference. The 7.125% 2031 notes do not automatically dominate the 6.000% 2033 notes: a higher coupon is not greater market compensation after price, call option and duration. The 4.625% and 4.875% 2029 subordinated series remain separate securities, not a coupon-average synthetic bond. A like-for-like comparison would require dated USD metrics matched for seniority, collateral/guarantor coverage, tenor, call-adjusted cash flows and trading liquidity; index or sector averages would remain benchmark context, not interchangeable security quotes.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 73","text":"A secured-over-subordinated structural bias is conditional, **not** an investment preference. If collateral reach and priority are verified and compensation is adequate, earlier/shorter secured exposure could reduce dependence on distant cash flows. If secured prices embed too little loss cushion while subordinate entry prices adequately compensate for verified residual-value risk, the value ordering could reverse. Neither side wins on the supplied evidence. Absence of March/June current inputs is not evidence of deteriorating spreads, financial results, access or recovery.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 75","text":"### Security comparison","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 77","text":"Every row has RV/compensation adequacy **Unclear** and decision **Requires More Work**; market date, executable price, YTW/OAS/DM and comparable quote quality are Not supplied for each. Amounts in Evidence are principal/gross obligations, not carrying value, market value or unused capacity. Issuer is Inc. unless otherwise identified; Holdings/subsidiary guarantees are summarized only to the extent supported by CP-4 and S1. Ordering below is for claim mapping, not a preference rank or a single universal waterfall.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 79","text":"| Instrument | Evidence | Compensation | Protection | Decision and gap |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 80","text":"|---|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 81","text":"| A/R securitization | 487 gross; 486 carrying; July 11, 2025 maturity; S1 pp.126,130 | SOFR +1.45%; not a traded DM | Domestic receivables collateral; TransDigm Receivables LLC pool and standard-undertaking framework per CP-4 | Requires More Work; asset-specific renewal/eligibility and residual reach need facility documents; not established as an available portfolio security |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 82","text":"| Revolver | 910 commitments, 843 reported available, 67 outstanding letters of credit; February 27, 2029; S1 pp.45,128,132 | SOFR +2.25%; unused fee 0.5%; not quoted return | Defined first-lien bank framework, but funded exposure, commitment claims and enforcement terms need facility/ICA | Requires More Work; 67 is the sourced LC amount, not inferred drawn borrowing; live availability/access conditions and acquisition/transfer eligibility Not supplied |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 83","text":"| Tranche I | 1,871; August 24, 2028; S1 p.132 | SOFR +2.75%, floating | Bank first-lien framework per CP-4; operative facility, security and voting details absent | Requires More Work; nearer tenor may reduce duration but increases nearer refinancing dependence; price/DM needed |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 84"