xecution, forecasts, accepted add-back challenge, live market evidence and portfolio inputs are Not supplied. CP-3 already absorbs conditional instrument comparison, and CP-4 addresses legal capacity conditions; neither establishes unused capacity, authenticated complete terms, numeric recovery or an executable preference. These omissions restrict the dependent conclusions, not the supported historical debate. The gate is **Ready with Limitations**, not Full Run or investment-ready completion.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 49","text":"## Findings","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 51","text":"### Committee conclusion","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 53","text":"The committee selects **Requires More Work**. Neither side establishes an implementable investment: the Bull supports improving historical operating cash and meaningful contractual protections, while the Bear establishes that actual extraction and conditional legal flexibility can keep that cash from becoming a creditor cushion. The Bear does not prove a liquidity failure, an unlawful payment or an inevitable restructuring. The decisive distinction is between operating capacity and retained, accessible resources. With neither a complete liquidity/downside bridge nor executable prices and portfolio evidence, a Starter Position would convert a plausible credit thesis into unsupported clearance. Avoid would likewise overstate the evidence by treating absent compensation and liquidity proof as demonstrated inadequacy. The conclusion preserves CP-3's Requires More Work/RV Unclear posture and CP-5's Restricted historical-use boundary.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 55","text":"### Committee challenge","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 57","text":"The Bull pitched three propositions: improving conversion supports debt service; 2033 guarantees and voting protections materially constrain adverse treatment; historical extensions and delayed term-loan/note bullets provide time to address future funding. The Bear attacked those exact propositions with the documented debt-funded dividend and rising carrying leverage, conditional restricted-payment/investment/release routes, and the earlier receivables-facility renewal requirement. The Bull answered with actual conversion, preserved payment/ranking rights and completed extensions\u2014not hypothetical support or unrestricted cash. The Chair sustained the historical operating evidence, partially mitigated the legal and tenor claims, and rejected the leap from any of them to implementation. This is a genuine challenged long thesis, not an attack on claims that cash was already unrestricted or securities already cheap; no producer made those claims.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 59","text":"### Portfolio decision boundary","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 61","text":"The absorbed portfolio posture is **Requires More Work**; portfolio debate winner **Neither wins**. No binding mandate constraint can be identified because the vehicle, mandate, holdings, limits, entry prices and proposed trade are Not supplied. This is an evidentiary implementation gate, not a demonstrated compliance breach or zero investment capacity. No security, size, include/add/trim/exit instruction or current investment clearance is approved. A structurally senior claim can be inferior value at the wrong price; a discounted junior claim could offer better compensation only with verified residual-value support. The actual case establishes neither ordering.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 63","text":"### Action Bias Determination","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 65","text":"Function 8: **Neither wins** under the method's winner definitions. Bull wins a bounded historical conversion proposition; Bear wins the cash-retention/policy objection, but cannot prove that downside overwhelms all mitigants. The Zero-Bound chain is a credible conditional mechanism, not a proved exhaustion path: shock magnitude, accessible starting resources, forecast response and funding outcomes are missing. Accordingly, its guardrail bars a high-conviction long without manufacturing an Avoid decision. The default Starter Position for proven cash durability, accessible liquidity, manageable maturities and fair-to-cheap RV does not apply: the latter three conditions have not been jointly established. Requires More Work is selected instead of Watchlist because usable liquidity, priced selection and portfolio implementation all remain decision-gating, not simply catalyst timing.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 67","text":"Final Action Bias: Requires More Work. The decision is driven by improving historical CFO and conversion alongside increased carrying leverage and the explicitly debt-funded September 2024 dividend declaration, because cash-generating capacity is not equivalent to cash retained and accessible for creditors. Conditional legal leakage and incomplete collateral/control evidence further limit protection, while absent executable quotes and mandate inputs prevent an investment conclusion. The main factor preventing a higher-conviction recommendation is unverified retained accessible liquidity after committed uses; market, legal and portfolio gates must also be satisfied before implementation.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 69","text":"### Analytical appendix \u2014 complete canonical registers","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 71","text":"### Function 2 \u2014 neutral pre-debate thesis map","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 73","text":"Evidence quality below concerns the stated fact or inference, not assurance over future outcomes. Strong = directly supported documentary/accounting evidence or source-backed checked handoff; Moderate = supported analysis/management evidence with limitations; Insufficient = required conclusion cannot be established. Repeated module citations are the same underlying evidence, not independent corroboration.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 75","text":"| Dimension | Neutral evidence inventory | Source / lineage | Quality and boundary |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 76","text":"|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 77","text":"| Cash-flow durability, margins and conversion | CFO 2,045/1,375/948; CFO less capex 1,880/1,236/829; FY2024/FY2023 conversion fractions 0.490055/0.405007; management estimates 55% aftermarket and 90% proprietary sales in FY2024 | CP-1 CF22/K02/K12, S1 pp.109/142; CP-1A B03/B04, S1 p.4; reported, calculated and management language kept separate | Strong historical money/ratios; Moderate durability inference; no sustainable FCF certification |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 78","text":"| Liquidity runway | Cash 6,261 at base date; dividends payable 4,216; October payments 4,216 common and 132 equivalents; revolver reported available 843 | CP-1 BS01/BS14/F06/SE03; S1 pp.105,45,146 | Strong reported observations; Insufficient accessible runway |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 79","text":"| Leverage / deleveraging | Carrying debt 24,880 versus 19,750; carrying leverage 5.962138x versus 5.817378x; mechanical cash-netted ratio falls | CP-1 K07/K09/K10; S1 pp.105/142; calculated | Strong historical arithmetic; netting not unrestricted cash or forward trajectory |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 80","text":"| Refinancing / maturities | Completed extensions; no term-loan/note bullet until November 2027, fiscal 2028; separate July 11, 2025 A/R facility maturity | CP-1 F/MAT; CP-1A X06/BF02; S1 pp.43,45\u201346,130,133 | Strong reported history; Insufficient dated future execution |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 81","text":"| Legal / covenants | 2033 payment guarantees, ranking/payment voting rights, conditional RP/debt permissions and releases | CP-4 F02\u2013F14; L \u00a7\u00a74.07,4.09,9.02,10,12 | Strong wording; Moderate application; no capacity certificate |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 82","text":"| Recovery / LGD | Combined issuer/guarantor summary exists; non-guarantor and asset-pool structural differences remain | CP-4 entity/control registers; CP-3 claim reach; S1 pp.44\u201345 | Strong summary scope; Insufficient asset-level values, allowed claims or recovery |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 83","text":"| Relative value | CP-3 RV Unclear; coupons, historical issue and call prices are not executable returns | CP-3 recommendation/security table; S1 p.46 | Insufficient quotes and comparable curves |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 84","text":"| Portfolio fit | No vehicle, holdings, mandate, risk budget, proposed trade or limits | Current input inventory; CP-3 portfolio section | Insufficient; no breach inferred |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 85","text":"| Sponsor / governance | Explicit debt-funded distribution; no current sponsor/control/support finding; reporting and extensions are counterevidence | CP-1A BF01/GT/O; S1 pp.131,146,56\u201358 | Strong historical action; Insufficient ownership/support/affiliate conclusion |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 86","text":"| Catalyst visibility | October settlement is known subsequent history; declarations, cash retention, legal certificates, renewal evidence and quotes are revisit signals | CP-1 SE02/SE03; CP-2/3 monitoring | Strong dated subsequent events; Insufficient new operating/investment catalyst |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 88","text":"**Central controversy:** Does a durable installed-base franchise generate resources retained and accessible to creditors, or do discretionary extraction, reinvestment and conditional legal flexibility keep debt service and refinancing dependent on continuing favorable operations? This question is not resolved by a larger gross cash balance or a senior-secured label.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 90","text":"### Function 3 \u2014 Bull opening: exactly three claims","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 92","text":"**B1 \u2014 Improved conversion is a real debt-service mitigant.** Evidence: CP-1 CF22/K02/K12 and CP-2 show annual CFO and pre-acquisition/distribution CFO less capex rising in FY2022\u2013FY2024; conversion to EBITDA As Defined improves. CP-1A B03/B04 supplies management's installed-base/aftermarket rationale, not contracted recurring revenue. Mechanic: repeat replacement consumption plus demonstrated collections and modest historical cash capex can fund interest and reinvestment before discretionary allocation. Credit implication: **Neutral \u2014 Stable**, for the historical servicing base, not Positive \u2014 Deleveraging. Monitoring: invalidate the durability inference if like-for-like margins cease converting to cash, inventory/receivables absorb more resources, or maintenance/integration needs consume the apparent surplus. Basis: S1 pp.4,109,142; CP-1 definitions retained.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 94","text":"**B2 \u2014 The 2033 package contains meaningful barriers to an overt adverse rewrite.** Evidence: L \u00a710.01 joint-and-several payment guarantees; \u00a79.02 affected-holder principal/payment/ranking protection and 66\u2154% for specified nonpermitted substantially-all collateral releases or materially adverse ICA changes; CP-4 F05 also identifies a junior-or-Permitted-Lien condition. Mechanic: direct recourse and class/affected-holder consents constrain an unconstrained majority priority rewrite, increasing the importance of enforcing actual contractual boundaries. Credit implication: **Neutral \u2014 Stable**, conditional legal protection, not a recovery floor. Monitoring: new release/designation, secured issuance, consent or ICA change; test actual terms, filings and entity reach rather than infer them from consolidated accounts. Basis: L pp.26\u201327 \u00a7\u00a79.02/10.01; CP-4 F05/F10/F14.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 96","text":"**B3 \u2014 Historical tenor management supplies time rather than an immediate term-loan/note bullet crisis.** Evidence: CP-1A X06/BF02 records completed repricing/extensions; S1 p.43 explicitly places the first tranche/note maturity in November 2027, fiscal 2028. CP-1 retains FY2025/FY2026/FY2027 scheduled long-term repayments excluding leases of 93/92/92, not a complete total-funding requirement. Mechanic: selected extensions and deferred bullets provide time for operating cash generation and proactive funding work; they do not themselves retire debt or prove repeat access. Credit implication: **Neutral \u2014 Stable** for historical tenor. Monitoring: A/R renewal/eligibility, amortization, new debt, quotes and actual refinancing terms. Basis: S1 pp.43,45\u201346,128\u2013133; CP-1 F/MAT; CP-1A BF02.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 98","text":"### Function 4 \u2014 T6A.4 Bear cross-examination: exactly three concrete attacks","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 100","text":"| Bull Claim Attacked | Bear Counter-Evidence | Fragility Vector | Legal / Covenant Exploit | Risk Mechanic | Credit Implication | What Would Prove Bear Wrong |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 101","text":"|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 102","text":"| B1: improved conversion supports servicing | CP-1 carrying leverage rises to 5.962138x from 5.817378x; FY2024 acquisitions use 2,347 and paid dividends/equivalents 2,038. S1 p.131 explicitly links September borrowing plus cash to the declaration; p.146 records October settlement. | Operating conversion can improve without retained cash; utilization/supply stress then meets a larger fixed-claim burden. | CP-4 F02/F06; L p.18 \u00a74.07 permits any RP if no continuing Default/EoD and legal pro forma FCCR exceeds 2.0x; certain compliant contractual commitments can survive later deterioration. | Actual distribution willingness, not merely unused permission, limits how much operating cash supports deleveraging. B1 survives only as operating capacity, not a sufficient cushion. | Negative \u2014 Leverage Increase | Comparable evidence of cash retained after maintenance, integration and commitments, accessible by obligor, accompanied by actual debt retirement; not a promise to stop distributions. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 103","text":"| B2: guarantees and consent rights materially constrain adverse treatment | CP-4 F06/F07/F10/F11 documents permitted investments/designations, conditional guarantee/lien releases and absent security/ICA evidence; L p.18 permits classification/combination and FMV designation treatment. | Value can leave direct recourse through permitted transactions without a forbidden amendment. | Permitted releases differ from the \u00a79.02 supermajority barrier for nonpermitted sweeping release; no need to assume a majority can override sacred ranking rights. | Payment rights can remain intact while reachable assets shrink or pari/local claims grow; therefore overt-rewrite protections do not establish retained collateral coverage. | Negative \u2014 Covenant Erosion | Complete executed package and transaction/entity evidence showing the relevant transfers/releases constrained and value retained in enforceable guarantee/collateral pools. Missing evidence alone does not prove leakage occurred. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 104","text":"| B3: deferred term-loan/note bullets provide time | CP-1 F07 reports July 11, 2025 A/R maturity, 487 gross drawn and 650 capacity; BS14/SE03 shows committed cash uses before that renewal. S1 p.45 reports 67 LCs and 843 revolver availability, not unrestricted cash. | A conditional funding/collection need can precede the bond wall, particularly after cash extraction or under weaker eligible receivables. | CP-4 describes non-recourse securitization pool/undertakings and no recurring numerical notes-maintenance test; no note-maintenance trigger forces early deleveraging simply because earnings fall. | Tenor relief is useful but not proof the business can bridge earlier renewal or accessibility needs; operational cash and funding eligibility must coexist. | Negative \u2014 Refinancing Risk | Actual scope-matched renewal/funding evidence and a complete accessible liquidity bridge through commitments, amortization and stress. No renewal failure is asserted from missing follow-up. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 106","text":"**Bear Zero-Bound attempt:** From the September 2024 base, weaker utilization, OEM disruption or a qualified-supplier interruption first reduces spares orders/deliverable shipments (CP-1A B10/B11/B14), then adverse mix and costs reduce operating earnings; slower receivables and excess inventory weaken CFO (CP-1 K03; CP-2 downside chain). Interest, reinvestment and committed distributions then compete for accessible resources. Additional borrowing could sustain operations while raising leverage; reduced receivable eligibility or an unrenewed facility could intensify refinancing pressure before the note bullets. Eventually a missed payment or qualifying cross-default could engage CP-4's actual notice/grace/remedy rules. Observable signals are orders/shipments, collection/inventory cash use, declared commitments, eligibility/renewal evidence and formal default notices. **The chain cannot be completed to exhaustion, breach, default timing or investor loss:** the shock magnitude, cost response, accessible starting cash, complete cash bridge, live facilities, valuation and entry price are Not supplied. CP-2A/CP-2D/CP-3C have not been silently executed.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 108","text":"**Legal-Control Test within these three attacks:** CP-4 F02/F03/F05\u2013F08/F10/F11/F14 links broad legal earnings adjustments to ratio debt/RP ability; Clause M's 35% post-adjustment cap and 24-month action window are not global caps on all adjustments. Debt and lien permission are separate; 5.25x applies to a specific permitted-lien route, not a universal maintenance ceiling. Incremental loan/MFN rights require absent facility terms. Investments, USub designation, transfers and permitted releases can change reach, but actual IP transfers, priming or uptiers are not established. General majority amendment is bounded by affected-holder ranking/payment rights and specified 66\u2154% consent. Missing ICA/security documents leave enforcement control and asset-level coverage unverified\u2014not disproved. This test supports a conditional risk channel, not an allegation of executed coercive LME.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 110","text":"**Bear conclusion:** Strong evidence defeats automatic cash-retention and unqualified protection inferences. It does not defeat the existence of improving operating cash, prove a cash shortfall, or establish that any security is inadequately compensated.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 112","text":"### Function 5 \u2014 matching Bull defenses","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 114","text":"| Attack | Specific Bull defense and mitigation | Rebuttal status / remaining limit |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 115","text":"|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 116","text":"| B1 attack | CP-1 FY2024 CFO is 2,045 after operating cash interest and taxes; K02 deducts the reported capex of 165 from CFO to give 1,880 before acquisitions and distributions. Conversion rises across all three years. Installed-base replacement demand and no FY2024/FY2023 program buybacks are relevant counterevidence (CP-1A B03/B04/X05). This preserves a cash-producing franchise, not cash retained after acquisitions/distributions. | Partially Rebutted. Bull cannot quantify accessible liquidity protection or erase the explicit funding-to-dividend link. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 117","text":"| B2 attack | L \u00a7\u00a79.02/10.01 provides actual payment/ranking consent protection and direct guarantees; CP-4 F05 retains the junior-or-permitted rule. FMV/RP designation conditions and release requirements mean borrower flexibility is not unlimited. These provisions matter to a proposed transaction even though they do not establish its asset coverage. | Partially Rebutted. Bull cannot authenticate perfection, ICA enforcement or asset-level coverage from the supplied summary. No numerical recovery defense is available. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 118","text":"| B3 attack | Completed extensions and the sourced first note date remain real. The A/R facility has conditional extension rights and the annual source reports revolver availability; these provide possible funding channels, not proof of failure. Correct November 2027/fiscal 2028 mapping preserves the actual tenor benefit. | Partially Rebutted. Historical availability and conditional extensions do not complete a dated funding bridge; future execution and live liquidity remain unproved. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 120","text":"### Function 6 \u2014 T6A.6 Chair nine-dimension evidence weighting","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 122","text":"Scores adjudicate the evidence on this bounded issue, not credit quality, probability or size. Scale: 1 Bull clearly superior, 2 Bull somewhat stronger, 3 balanced/unresolved, 4 Bear somewhat stronger, 5 Bear clearly superior. Missing dimensions are unscored, never assigned neutral 3 by default. Overall **Provisional; no partial average**.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 124","text":"| Dimension | Score (1-5) | Bull Evidence | Bear Evidence | Chair Assessment |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 125","text":"|---|---|---|---|---|","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 126","text":"| Cash-flow durability | 2 | CP-1 CF22/K02/K12 actual improving conversion; CP-1A B03/B04 demand mechanism | CP-1 K03 cash absorption, CF24/CF28 allocation; untested sustainable earnings | Bull stronger on historical cash-producing ability, not on retained or stressed FCF. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 127","text":"| Downside pathway severity | Unscored \u2014 stress calibration Not supplied | Historical margins and conversion | Conditional causal chain with qualified supply/utilization channels | Mechanism credible; loss severity cannot be adjudicated without forecasts, cost response and liquidity. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 128","text":"| Liquidity runway | Unscored \u2014 accessible bridge Not supplied | Reported cash and revolver availability | Committed subsequent uses and conditional A/R funding | Neither usable buffer nor exhaustion is established. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 129","text":"| Refinancing/maturity risk | 3 | Actual extensions and first term-loan/note bullet in fiscal 2028 | Earlier A/R renewal and increased debt | Supported competing tenor/renewal facts; forward execution unresolved, not a current market-access grade. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 130","text":"| Legal/covenant control | 4 | Guarantees, junior-or-permitted liens and sacred rights | Conditional leakage/designation/release and broad legal adjustments | Bear somewhat stronger on retention/control limits; protections remain meaningful and transaction-specific. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 131","text":"| Recovery/LGD protection | Unscored \u2014 values/claims/asset coverage Not supplied | Guarantees and combined issuer/guarantor summary | Non-guarantor/pool structure, release and ICA gaps | No recovery floor or impairment amount follows from either case. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 132","text":"| Sponsor/governance alignment | 4 | Reporting transpar