des current portion | Principal, carrying debt, and legal indebtedness are not interchangeable. Analytical K07 uses reported carrying amounts; finance leases included once. S1 pp.105, 126\u2013127. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 447","text":"| Lease wording | S1 p.131 calls 262 / 193 finance lease value \u201cnet of the current portion\u201d; p.148 explicitly splits total 262 / 193 into current 6 / 5 and long-term 256 / 188 | Use explicit Note 17 classification with p.126's total for accounting; retain narrative wording inconsistency. Do not add current leases again. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 448","text":"| Cash-flow bridge changes | CB02 adds back 272 / 415, versus the absolute CF15\u2013CF21 block totals 302 / 431 | Distinct reported bridge versus calculated complete cash-flow block. Differences 30 / 16 are not forced to zero or called a working-capital error. Detailed reclassification explanation remains open. S1 pp.54, 109. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 449","text":"| Dividends | CF28 cash paid, IS21 per-share declarations, BS14 accrual, EQ23 equity charge and Note 16 common/option amounts have different scopes/timing | No assumption of zero dividends in FY2023: CF28 reports cash payments despite IS21's common-dividend dash. Equity-versus-note residual is disclosed in T4.19. |","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 451","text":"### Evidence-based annual read-through","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 453","text":"**Operating performance.** TransDigm's reported revenue and operating income both increased from FY2023 to FY2024 (IS01, IS06); K13 calculates increases of 1,355 and 608, with growth fractions 0.205771 and 0.208005. Gross and operating margins rose on the calculated K04\u2013K05 definitions. All three segment revenue totals increased (SG04, SG08, SG09); SG01\u2013SG07 show the relevant commercial/OEM, aftermarket and defense rows without attributing the consolidated increase to an untested price/volume/organic cause. The source explains that segments reflect internal performance reporting and corporate reconciliation, not independent legal obligors (S1 pp.140\u2013142). No forecast follows from these historical comparisons.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 455","text":"**Cash conversion.** CFO increased by 670 (K13; CF22); the complete source changes-in-assets/liabilities block remained a cash use, but its use narrowed by 129 (K03/K13). K12 conversion improved, and K02 CFO less capex increased. CF24 acquisitions and CF28 distributions are outside that FCF definition, so this does not establish cash available for debt paydown. Cash interest CF43 is distinct from IS07 and CB03, while tax paid CF44 is distinct from IS11; neither accrual earnings nor the issuer's EBITDA adjustment bridge is a substitute for cash flows. Source non-GAAP cautions explicitly identify interest, taxes, replacement expenditure and cash integration costs as omitted burdens (S1 p.52).","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 457","text":"**Funding and leverage.** K07 carrying debt increased by 5,130 (K13), while reported cash CF42 increased and the cash-netted K10 multiple declined. Gross carrying leverage K09 nevertheless increased: the two directions are not contradictory because cash netting changes the numerator. The liquidity implication of that netting is restricted: BS14/SE01 identifies a declared payment obligation and SE03 records its October settlement. S1 p.131 explicitly says the fourth-quarter notes and term-loan proceeds, together with cash on hand, were used to fund the special-dividend declaration. S1 p.128 separately identifies 2031 notes/Tranche J proceeds and cash as financing the CPI Electron Device acquisition. These are documented funding links, not an inference from simultaneous debt and dividends. Reported positive financing CF38 supported the historical cash rollforward; no claim that all base-date cash was accessible, unrestricted or permanent is made.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 459","text":"**Coverage and quality.** Operating-income/net-interest coverage K11 improved, but it is an accounting ratio using net interest, not cash coverage or a covenant headroom test. EB06\u2013EB09 include compensation, financing and acquisition-related adjustments across comparative periods; CP-1D must test recurrence and cash consequences rather than accepting their add-back status. S1 p.143 discloses liability-based awards and recurring measurement; S1 p.52 warns of cash integration cost exclusions. No independent adjusted earnings restatement is presented here.","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 461","text":"## Calculations","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 463","text":"### T4.9 \u2014 Calculation traces and T4.19 reconciliations","formula":null,"cached_value":null,"hidden":false,"data_type":null,"number_format":null,"note":null},{"locator":"line 465","text":"All new arithmetic used the supplied Decimal-38 `calculate` kernel. Signed source lexemes were translated to decimal operands only in calculations: commas removed; parentheses negative; expense magnitudes subtracted where appropriate. Results below are calculated, not source-printed facts. R