n any tranche of term loans or notes until November 2027 (fiscal 2028).\u201d S1 p.46 reports D03's 2,650 principal due November 15, 2027. That date falls in fiscal 2028, so it does not conflict with the fiscal 2027 bucket of 92 on p.133. All reported repayment rows remain unchanged. This correction does not establish a complete instrument/amortization allocation by fiscal bucket; no amounts are moved and no issuer reconciliation is requested solely for the withdrawn conflict."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C471","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 360"},{"name":"Quote","value":"All monetary amounts USD millions. FY2022 columns are not supplied in the reviewed Note 17 tables; no lease estimate is filled."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C472","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 385"},{"name":"Quote","value":"At September 30, 2024, remaining operating/finance lease terms are 5.4years / 21.0 years and discount rates 6.1% / 7.0%, respectively (S1 p.148; source spelling retained for 5.4years)."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C473","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 399"},{"name":"Quote","value":"All liability lines BS11\u2013BS20 were reviewed for funding relevance, not just financial debt. Material non-debt stories are as follows:"},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C474","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 412"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Reported rows cite source; calculated rows reference the traces below. Monetary values USD millions; margins/conversions are fractions, not percentages. Rounded analytical ratios are displayed to six decimal places, with unrounded Decimal-38 outputs retained in the calculation execution record. Unprovided FY2022 balance-dependent quantities and ordinary reported EBITDA are blank; reasons follow the table."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C475","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 436"},{"name":"Quote","value":"FY2022 K07\u2013K10 cannot be calculated from the supplied primary balance sheets; no debt balance is inferred from cash-flow issuance/repayments. FCF is a bounded analyst definition, not issuer reported FCF, FFO, maintenance FCF, cash available for dividends, or debt-service capacity. No maintenance/growth split, adjusted CFO, FFO, covenant headroom, unrestricted cash, or current liquidity is supplied by these calculations."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C476","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 453"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Operating performance.** TransDigm's reported revenue and operating income both increased from FY2023 to FY2024 (IS01, IS06); K13 calculates increases of 1,355 and 608, with growth fractions 0.205771 and 0.208005. Gross and operating margins rose on the calculated K04\u2013K05 definitions. All three segment revenue totals increased (SG04, SG08, SG09); SG01\u2013SG07 show the relevant commercial/OEM, aftermarket and defense rows without attributing the consolidated increase to an untested price/volume/organic cause. The source explains that segments reflect internal performance reporting and corporate reconciliation, not independent legal obligors (S1 pp.140\u2013142). No forecast follows from these historical comparisons."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C477","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 455"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Cash conversion.** CFO increased by 670 (K13; CF22); the complete source changes-in-assets/liabilities block remained a cash use, but its use narrowed by 129 (K03/K13). K12 conversion improved, and K02 CFO less capex increased. CF24 acquisitions and CF28 distributions are outside that FCF definition, so this does not establish cash available for debt paydown. Cash interest CF43 is distinct from IS07 and CB03, while tax paid CF44 is distinct from IS11; neither accrual earnings nor the issuer's EBITDA adjustment bridge is a substitute for cash flows. Source non-GAAP cautions explicitly identify interest, taxes, replacement expenditure and cash integration costs as omitted burdens (S1 p.52)."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C478","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 457"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Funding and leverage.** K07 carrying debt increased by 5,130 (K13), while reported cash CF42 increased and the cash-netted K10 multiple declined. Gross carrying leverage K09 nevertheless increased: the two directions are not contradictory because cash netting changes the numerator. The liquidity implication of that netting is restricted: BS14/SE01 identifies a declared payment obligation and SE03 records its October settlement. S1 p.131 explicitly says the fourth-quarter notes and term-loan proceeds, together with cash on hand, were used to fund the special-dividend declaration. S1 p.128 separately identifies 2031 notes/Tranche J proceeds and cash as financing the CPI Electron Device acquisition. These are documented funding links, not an inference from simultaneous debt and dividends. Reported positive financing CF38 supported the historical cash rollforward; no claim that all base-date cash was accessible, unrestricted or permanent is made."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C479","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 459"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Coverage and quality.** Operating-income/net-interest coverage K11 improved, but it is an accounting ratio using net interest, not cash coverage or a covenant headroom test. EB06\u2013EB09 include compensation, financing and acquisition-related adjustments across comparative periods; CP-1D must test recurrence and cash consequences rather than accepting their add-back status. S1 p.143 discloses liability-based awards and recurring measurement; S1 p.52 warns of cash integration cost exclusions. No independent adjusted earnings restatement is presented here."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C480","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 465"},{"name":"Quote","value":"All new arithmetic used the supplied Decimal-38 `calculate` kernel. Signed source lexemes were translated to decimal operands only in calculations: commas removed; parentheses negative; expense magnitudes subtracted where appropriate. Results below are calculated, not source-printed facts. Ratios require positive denominators, which are present for every displayed ratio. All monetary operands are consolidated USD millions, and same-year annual flows are not mixed with post-period events. Balance-dependent ratios pair the year-end instant with that fiscal year's duration. No ratio is represented as a legal test."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"2ec4b36a3bec9bd872ff53b9c31628ab59551a3eed5ed7c11501e06006b42891"}]},{"ref_id":"C481","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-1"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 482"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Blank numeric FY2022 cells in K07\u2013K10 mean Not cal