et-relative grade. Confidence is Medium for credit implications and higher for the directly read wording; package-wide execution/compliance conclusions are not supported."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C886","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 50"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Amounts are USD millions at September 30, 2024 unless otherwise stated. Accounting carrying value is not a legal claim amount, lien amount or recovery value. CP-1 remains canonical for financial normalization."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C887","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 62"},{"name":"Quote","value":"S1 pp.44\u201345 supplies summarized combined financial data for TD Group, TransDigm Inc. and other guarantors, including TransDigm UK: non-issuer/non-guarantor subsidiaries are excluded, intercompany balances and transactions among included entities are eliminated, and balances/dealings with excluded entities are separately presented. Guarantor financial information is therefore not wholly absent. This combined summary is not an individual entity/collateral/perfection/value map or an allowed-claims waterfall; those gaps remain."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C888","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 64"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The accounting perimeter is TD Group and controlled subsidiaries including NCI. The legal operating perimeter is the Company and its **Restricted Subsidiaries**, with Holdings separately guaranteeing and contributing to certain definitions. Neither segments nor the full consolidation prove obligor coverage. Definitions of Restricted/Unrestricted Subsidiary, Guarantor, Grantor and Securitization Entity determine reach (L pp.7,11\u201312 \u00a7\u00a71.01). Non-guarantor local creditors have first access to their entity's assets before an upstream equity residual reaches note obligors; this is structural subordination, distinct from contractual payment subordination and lien ranking."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C889","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 68"},{"name":"Quote","value":"This is the clause-specific 14-family register. Each numbered family has its own boundary, conditions and missing inputs; the supplementary registers retain capacity, remedies and structural detail. Quoted thresholds are contractual terms, not measured results. No missing usage is treated as zero."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C890","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 89"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Definitions change capacity, not just reported leverage.** L p.5 L410\u2013L424 defines FCCR as legal EBITDA over Fixed Charges for four full quarters with internal statements, pro forma financing and acquisitions/dispositions, transaction-date floating rates and swap effects. Fixed Charges adds tax-grossed preferred dividends to defined interest. Defined interest excludes financing-fee amortization, bridge/commitment fees, qualified securitization costs and prepayment premiums, while adding capitalized interest and capital-lease interest. EBITDA includes expansive transaction, restructuring, dividend-equivalent and projected-savings adjustments. Clause M's 35% limit is neither a global cap on all EBITDA add-backs nor a cap on every pro forma acquisition adjustment: L421\u2013L422 separately permits officer-good-faith acquisition calculations and reasonably determined operating expense reductions. The no-duplication and specified exclusions still matter; the document is not permission to add the same amount twice. Wider earnings and narrower fixed charges can make ratio debt and distributions easier before actual cash savings arrive, increasing debt-service sensitivity and weakening the residual asset cushion. Monitor adjustment categories, actual realization and transaction-date rate inputs, not the accounting multiple."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C891","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 91"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Debt and lien permissions are separate.** L p.18 \u00a74.09 L1295 says **\u201cgreater than 2.0 to 1.0\u201d**, not greater than or equal. L p.10 L715 says **\u201cshall not exceed 5.25 to 1.00\u201d** for the specific (xxxi) Ratio Indebtedness lien route. Permitted Liens (iii) covers Bank Indebtedness; (xx) links purchase-money and additional-debt baskets to asset-specific/collateral-only limits; (xxi) confines foreign-sub liens to foreign-sub assets. Accordingly, 5.25 is not a blanket secured leverage maintenance ceiling or a condition on every lien. Permitted-debt reclassification can refresh fixed baskets; acquisition debt can use an improved-FCCR alternative even without satisfying the USD1 ratio-debt test. These provisions can permit further pari claims or locally senior funding without a new breach, but actual priming is not established. The contrary case is \u00a74.12's express junior-or-permitted requirement and \u00a79.02's affected-holder ranking protection. A proposed priority change must satisfy those boundaries and the missing ICA, rather than relying on a generic majority-vote claim."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C892","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 93"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Leakage can occur before default and may outlast deteriorating tests.** \u00a74.07 L1265 permits **\u201cany Restricted Payment\u201d** subject to no continuing Default/EoD and pro forma FCCR exceeding 2.0x. L1272 preserves certain payments contractually committed while conditions held. The builder basket therefore is not the sole potential distribution constraint. Permitted Investments can reach non-guarantors, and designation of a guarantor as Unrestricted can release its guarantee and liens under \u00a7\u00a710.07(c),12.07(f), subject to designation and RP conditions. Asset-sale exclusions, \u00a75.01's intragroup carveout and affiliate carveouts mean a transfer may avoid one covenant yet remain subject to others. No categorical IP-transfer prohibition is identified in the supplied indenture; this is a conditional route, not a finding that material IP has been transferred. Without an entity/IP schedule, valuation and usage ledger its amount is Not calculable. These mechanics can reduce creditors' reachable value without an immediate payment default; monitor designations, intragroup transfers, RP commitments and releases as well as reported dividends."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C893","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 95"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**The historical distribution demonstrates willingness, not a capacity opinion.** S1 p.131 expressly links September notes and Tranche L proceeds plus existing cash to the USD75/share declaration and eligible option equivalents. S1 p.146 records USD4,216 million common dividends accrued at September 30 and USD4,216 million common plus USD132 million equivalent payments in **October 2024**. The latter are subsequent cash uses, not FY2024 cash flow. Neither the funding link nor the issuer compliance statement on p.132 identifies the precise \u00a74.07 route, verifies conditions at declaration/commitment or proves residual capacity. A general compliance assertion is not the missing transaction certificate. Retain CP-1A BF01 as extraction behavior, not unlawful payment or coercive LME evidence."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C894","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 97"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Asset-sale protection is real but delayed and qualified.** FMV consideration and conditional cash requirements, reinvestment/application deadlines, and a pro rata 100%-plus-interest offer protect noteholders where \u00a74.10 applies. Countervailing flexibility includes deemed cash (assumed liabilities, instruments converted within 180 days and designated noncash consideration), long reinvestment periods, net-proceeds deductions, use to repay secured or non-guarantor debt, and return of untendered residual to permitted general purposes. The special productive-assets alternative requires substitute Productive Assets promptly to become Collateral where sold assets were collateral (L1317). This supports collateral continuity in that path, but is not a universal requirement that all proceeds immediately repay these Notes. Do not collapse asset-sales proceeds into near-term note amortization."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C895","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 99"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Guarantees improve direct recourse but are neither universal nor permanent.** \u00a710.01 promises unconditional, irrevocable, joint-and-several payment/performance, not merely collection, with reinstatement for rescinded payments; \u00a710.02 limits enforceability by fraudulent-transfer law. The executed signer list includes CPI, Calspan, Raptor entities and TransDigm UK, among others (L pp.31\u201332), but is not a current exhaustive ownership/value schedule. \u00a74.17's facility limb and separate >=200 capital-markets limb can capture new obligors, with 20-Business-Day accession; \u00a712.04 links required guarantee accession to security/ICA joinder. \u00a710.07 nonetheless releases on permitted external disposals, compliant USub designation, immateriality under its conditions, release from specified triggering debt, or funded discharge/defeasance. Immaterial Domestic Restricted Subsidiary requires both \u003c=2.5% EBITDA and \u003c=2.5% assets, using the specified >45-day reporting lag (L p.7 L535); no aggregate immateriality cap is stated in that definition. A non-guarantor is not the same as an Unrestricted Subsidiary, and a foreign subsidiary is not automatically outside every guarantee: TransDigm UK is expressly excluded from the defined Foreign Restricted Subsidiary category and signs here."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C896","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 101"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Security documentation determines realized control.** Collateral excludes the absent Security Agreement's Excluded Collateral (L p.4 L389). \u00a712.03 conditions some further collateralization on corresponding facility requirements; \u00a712.06 provides commercially reasonable perfection efforts and a 90-day outside period, not evidence those filings were completed. \u00a712.07(e)(B) follows specified Credit Agreement Collateral Agent releases, but excludes the stated full-cash facility discharge outside foreclosure/remedies; it is not an automatic release whenever the facility is repaid. \u00a712.07(e)(A) can release collateral transferred outside Company/Holdings/Guarantors in a permitted transaction, potentially including a restricted non-guarantor recipient, subject to full operative conditions. Permitted automatic releases differ from amendments releasing substantially all collateral outside the documents. Certificates and opinions are required to evidence requested releases; none is supplied here."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C897","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 103"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**LME/control protection is mixed rather than absent.** \u00a79.02 expressly contemplates consents in tender/exchange offers; general covenant changes can bind dissenters by majority. However, affected-holder protections include principal, fixed maturity, redemption terms, interest/payment timing, currency, payment suit, adversely changed ranking and specified post-trigger change-of-control obligations. L p.27 L1857 protects changes **\u201caffecting the subordination or ranking of the Notes or the Guarantees\u201d** adverse to holders. A materially adverse ICA modification or unauthorized all/substantially all collateral release needs 66\u2154%, not merely majority. \u00a72.09 excludes issuer/control-affiliate votes, with trustee actual-knowledge protection. \u00a76.06 prohibits using the indenture to obtain preference over another holder; \u00a76.07 preserves individual due-payment suits. These are meaningful opposite-case barriers. They do not prove that every non-pro-rata exchange, open-market purchase or asset-based transaction is prohibited, or that a majority can validly override every priority right. No executed coercive LME, uptier or drop-down is established by the supplied actions."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C898","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 109"},{"name":"Quote","value":"All amounts below are documentary USD-million parameters, not unused capacity. Current legal inputs, usage and remaining capacity for every row are **Not supplied / Not calculable because no legal reconciliation and election/use ledger is provided**. Permissions may overlap or reclassify; they are not summed. Definitions and operative conditions control over this compressed register."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C899","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 152"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Payment/nonpayment and notice conditions must not be conflated. Interest gets 30 days (\u00a76.01(a)); principal and due tender payments do not receive that same grace (\u00a76.01(b)). Other covenants require notice from trustee or 25% holders and 60 days, reporting 180 days; \u00a75.01 requires notice but not that passage of time (\u00a76.01(c)). Cross-debt default is a **final-maturity payment failure or acceleration**, not every debt covenant breach; threshold is at least USD50 million and excludes Securitization Entities in that limb. Final/nonappealable judgments use **in excess of** USD50 million and a 60-day unpaid/unstayed test. Collateral failure above USD50 million has a 60-day persistence limb, while a court pleading repudiating validity is separately covered (\u00a76.01(h)). The Company or Significant Subsidiary insolvency events are covered, but automatic acceleration under the controlling \u00a76.02 applies to **Company** bankruptcy events; others use the stated declaration mechanism. Majority can rescind acceleration under conditions and waive nonpayment-excepted past defaults; it cannot simply waive continuing ordinary payment defaults for all dissenters (\u00a7\u00a76.02,6.04,6.07)."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C900","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 154"},{"name":"Quote","value":"\u00a74.19 requires both agencies' investment-grade ratings and no continuing Default for suspension. Suspended provisions include RP, upstream restrictions, incurrence, asset sales, affiliates, business, guarantees, preferred stock, impairment and specified merger ratio condition; **liens and change-of-control remain outside that list**. Reversion is prospective, with suspension-period debt allocated under its specified treatment, no retroactive breach solely for suspension-period acts and a 30-day catch-up guarantee accession. Actual suspension notices/ratings are Not supplied; no conclusion that covenants were switched off is made."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C901","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 156"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Article VIII defeasance is different from ratings suspension: irrevocable USD cash/noncallable government-securities funding sufficient in independent accountants' opinion, tax/legal opinions, officers' certificates, no-default and specified 91-day bankruptcy conditions are required. Covenant defeasance releases the listed covenants including lien/change-of-control obligations and specified cross-default/judgment events; legal defeasance discharges broader obligations with surviving trust-payment rights. Discharge under \u00a78.06 has its own cancellation/due-within-one-year funding conditions. These are not unfunded unilateral covenant escapes, and no exercise is evidenced."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C902","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 160"},{"name":"Quote","value":"PD and LGD are qualitative transmission channels, not estimated probabilities or recovery percentages. All rows are Analyst Interpretation grounded in the referenced documentary provisions."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C903","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 170"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Time-aware downside:** an aerospace utilization/supply shock in CP-2 first reduces deliverable shipments or mix, then cash collection and legal earnings. There is no automatic numerical notes-maintenance breach solely because EBITDA falls. New incurrence/RP ability may tighten at transaction dates, while previously compliant contractual RP commitments may still drain cash; LCA tests may already have been locked at signing. If refinancing/receivables liquidity becomes insufficient, a missed payment, cross-final-maturity failure or acceleration can engage Article VI after its actual notice/grace rules. Enforcement then moves through agents and the missing ICA, with permitted releases and competing liens determining reachable value. Observable triggers are transaction certificates, commitment dates, liquidity events, formal notices, collateral releases and agent directions\u2014not an invented covenant breach date or forecast."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C904","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 172"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The strongest creditor-friendly case would win if complete documents and certificates showed ample tested coverage using realized cash earnings, restricted unused leakage, retained collateral/guarantor value and enforceable collective controls. Historical business resilience, successful tenor extensions and reporting transparency in CP-1A/CP-2 support that possibility, but do not establish those legal facts. Conversely, broad permissions alone do not establish an actual adverse LME. This distinction reduces confidence in implementation, not confidence that the quoted conditions exist."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C905","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 186"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Market-norm and third-party covenant-review comparison is limited because no supported comparative source was provided. The rubric's score labels are analytical categories, not evidence that this document is better/worse than a dated bond peer cohort. No independent confidence-score script or unavailable local validation is claimed; the source/instruction submission check is separate from host evidence review."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C906","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 206"},{"name":"Quote","value":"New direct S1 pp.43\u201346 review supplies the exact annual-reported note maturities (p.46): 5.50% 2027 notes November 15, 2027; 6.75% 2028 notes August 15, 2028; 4.625% 2029 notes January 15, 2029; 6.375% 2029 notes March 1, 2029; 4.875% 2029 notes May 1, 2029; 6.875% 2030 notes December 15, 2030; 7.125% 2031 notes December 1, 2031; 6.625% 2032 notes March 1, 2032; 6.00% 2033 notes January 15, 2033. Amounts/rates are unchanged; no call schedules are inferred from maturities. These reported dates are not unavailable. Annual-reported January 15, 2033 remains distinct from authentication of the supplied blank note form."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C907","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 208"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Corrected CP-1 MAT01\u2013MAT06 retains S1 p.133 reported long-term debt repayments excluding finance leases (USD millions): FY2025 93, FY2026 92, FY2027 92, FY2028 6,637, FY2029 4,768, thereafter 12,637. Short-term A/R securitization remains separate. The p.43 explicit November 2027/fiscal 2028 mapping and p.46 November 15, 2027 date withdraw the prior host/model conflict without moving any amount or establishing a full instrument/amortization allocation."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C908","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 210"},{"name":"Quote","value":"No new financial arithmetic was performed. Documentary basket amounts, ratios, deadlines and prices in Findings are extracted terms, not computed headroom. Provisional rubric scores are qualitative judgments under the supplied method, not an aggregate tool-generated financial result."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C909","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 212"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Retained CP-1 quantities: consolidated carrying debt September 30, 2024/2023 **24,880/19,750** USD million (K07); reported cash **6,261/3,472** (BS01); reported annual EBITDA As Defined FY2024/FY2023/FY2022 **4,173/3,395/2,646** (SG16); analyst carrying-debt/EBITDA As Defined **5.962138/5.817378** for 2024/2023 (K09); mechanical cash-netted multiples **4.461778/4.794698** (K10). These values retain CP-1's cited S1 pp.105,126\u2013127,142 and definitions. They are not used as legal test operands. FY2022 balance-dependent leverage is Not calculable because a debt instant is Not supplied. No zero substitutes for a missing year or usage."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C910","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 224"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Financial accounting remains separate from legal definitions even when both cite GAAP. The lack of capacity calculations is a required-input gap, not zero capacity, adverse evidence or proof of no headroom."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C911","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 230"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The executed full indenture is supplied and reviewed; it is **not** a missing input. Remaining gaps prevent a whole-package opinion, exact available capacity, perfection certification and security-selection implementation. The most material missing evidence is the controlling ICA/security/facility package and contemporaneous transaction-level calculation/election ledger. These gaps should be resolved by targeted requests, not by extrapolating the annual report or requesting the supplied indenture again."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C912","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 245"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Missing data is not misconduct, insolvency, absence of protection or refusal of support. No equity cure, support commitment, legal opinion or compliance certificate was invented. No recovery percentage, probability of default, forecast cash balance or market access conclusion was derived."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"3d39b8424f070064d992a2534bf0ef355ffbde34cd550222bb2adb97ac41e72e"}]},{"ref_id":"C913","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-4"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 249"},{"name":"Quote","value":"After host source/instruction review of this retained CP-4 artifact, **CP-6 is the next requested module**, not an automatically executed step. It must consume this actual response together with the current CP-0, CP-1, CP-1A and CP-2 handoffs and their exact identities. CP-6 must also review corrected CP-5 when available; no CP-5 handoff is supplied here. Its three prior instruction-context false positives stay withdrawn, and the maturity-conflict finding is withdrawn as a host/model calendar-fiscal err