sis, not a security recommendation. The request supplies these artifacts as the current analytical inputs; this module does not independently certify their prior host acceptance."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C996","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 31"},{"name":"Quote","value":"`list_sources` reanchored the following exact pinned identities. S1 means one-based PDF pages of `S1-annual-report.pdf`. L means tool text pages of `legal-text`, not original legal PDF pagination. S1 and its text aid are one logical annual source, not independent corroboration."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C997","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 42"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Other pinned method identities remain inventoried in current CP-0; they add no market or issuer evidence to this module. Source-embedded workflow commands are not authority to change current instructions. No enterprise connector, quote service, portfolio workbook, script execution or visual tool is supplied in this run. No market-source retrieval, independent confidence script, recovery-waterfall script or visual/PDF-fidelity check is claimed. The source-tool submission check is separate from host evidence review."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C998","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 44"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Accounting perimeter is TD Group and controlled subsidiaries, including NCI and eliminated intercompany balances. Legal issuer is TransDigm Inc.; Holdings is TD Group; restricted group, guarantors, grantors and securitization entities are separate legal concepts. Monetary quantities are **USD millions** unless expressly coupon, spread, price percentage, share quantity or ratio. FY durations are October\u2013September; debt/cash quantities below are September 30, 2024 instants unless stated otherwise. EY's source reports dated November 7, 2024 are later than the accounting base; no timely-availability inference is made."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C999","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 50"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Requires More Work across the identified securities; no forced ranking.** CP-2's installed-base replacement-demand thesis supports potential debt-service durability, but CP-1 and CP-1A show that improving operations coexisted with increased debt and a documented debt-funded equity payout. CP-4 identifies meaningful 2033 payment, guarantee and voting protection alongside conditional leakage and debt-incurrence flexibility. Together, these favor examining reachable assets and retained cash rather than selecting by coupon or maturity alone. They do not establish a winning security: entry prices, comparable compensation, trading liquidity and complete priority evidence are absent. A secured claim can have better downside reach yet offer inferior value at an excessive price; a subordinated claim can offer sufficient compensation only if its price, residual-value support and legal terms substantiate that case."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1000","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 54"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The following is a qualitative factor assessment, not a new fundamental model or agency rating. Governing scorecard weights and sufficient evidence for a weighted composite are Not supplied; composite and credit tier are **Not Scorable**, not inferred from CP-1A's separate governance rubric or CP-4's provisional legal score. No numerical override or ranking penalty is applied to missing evidence."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1001","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 65"},{"name":"Quote","value":"CP-1's retained annual CFO less capex is 1,880/1,236/829 in FY2024/FY2023/FY2022, before acquisitions and distributions. Acquisitions net of cash acquired were cash outflows 2,347/762/437, and dividends/equivalents paid were 2,038/38/1,091 (CF22\u2013CF24/CF28; S1 p.109). Thus E1/E2 support operating capacity, not automatic cash available to retire securities. No acquired full-year earnings, maintenance-capex split or accepted add-back restatement is invented."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1002","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 69"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**RV is Unclear for every instrument.** Coupons and contractual SOFR margins are known in the annual source, but neither is an executable yield, OAS, YTW or discount margin. September 2024 issuance at par for the 2033 notes and historical issue discounts elsewhere are transaction facts, not September 30 closing quotes and not November 2026 trading levels. No bid/ask, quote timestamp, accrued interest, dealer depth, traded volume or comparable market curve is supplied. Accordingly, there is no supported cheap/fair/rich label, peer spread differential or spread-based preference."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1003","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 71"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The conditional comparison is still substantive. All identified debt is USD reported, but fixed notes and floating loans have different rate risk, reset conventions, maturity and optionality. I/K carry SOFR plus 2.75%; J/L plus 2.50% in the base-date annual terms. That does not prove I/K offer better return: different prices, tenor, amortization, repricing rights and loan documents can offset the margin difference. The 7.125% 2031 notes do not automatically dominate the 6.000% 2033 notes: a higher coupon is not greater market compensation after price, call option and duration. The 4.625% and 4.875% 2029 subordinated series remain separate securities, not a coupon-average synthetic bond. A like-for-like comparison would require dated USD metrics matched for seniority, collateral/guarantor coverage, tenor, call-adjusted cash flows and trading liquidity; index or sector averages would remain benchmark context, not interchangeable security quotes."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1004","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 73"},{"name":"Quote","value":"A secured-over-subordinated structural bias is conditional, **not** an investment preference. If collateral reach and priority are verified and compensation is adequate, earlier/shorter secured exposure could reduce dependence on distant cash flows. If secured prices embed too little loss cushion while subordinate entry prices adequately compensate for verified residual-value risk, the value ordering could reverse. Neither side wins on the supplied evidence. Absence of March/June current inputs is not evidence of deteriorating spreads, financial results, access or recovery."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1005","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 77"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Every row has RV/compensation adequacy **Unclear** and decision **Requires More Work**; market date, executable price, YTW/OAS/DM and comparable quote quality are Not supplied for each. Amounts in Evidence are principal/gross obligations, not carrying value, market value or unused capacity. Issuer is Inc. unless otherwise identified; Holdings/subsidiary guarantees are summarized only to the extent supported by CP-4 and S1. Ordering below is for claim mapping, not a preference rank or a single universal waterfall."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1006","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 99"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The redeemed 6.25% secured 2026 notes (4,400) and 7.50% subordinated 2027 notes (550) are historical transactions, not September 30, 2024 outstanding securities (S1 pp.129\u2013130). They must not be reintroduced into the investment universe or maturity wall."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1007","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 103"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Note 10 reported long-term debt maturity schedule, excluding finance leases**, S1 p.133, at September 30, 2024. This is not a fully instrument-reconciled wall. All entries are source-reported, not independently validated instrument/amortization allocations. The earlier FY2027 withholding is withdrawn as a host/model calendar-fiscal error, not an issuer inconsistency. No carrying balances are plotted as principal and no maturity chart is produced."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1008","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 114"},{"name":"Quote","value":"S1 p.43 explicitly states: \u201cThere is no maturity on any tranche of term loans or notes until November 2027 (fiscal 2028).\u201d S1 p.46 reports **2,650 principal of 5.50% senior subordinated notes due November 15, 2027**. That date falls in fiscal 2028 and does not conflict with p.133's **92** fiscal-2027 bucket. The alleged conflict and issuer-reconciliation request motivated solely by it are withdrawn as a host/model calendar-fiscal error. No reported amount is changed or reassigned. The p.133 schedule totals 24,319; aggregate reconciliation and correct date mapping do not establish a full instrument/amortization allocation. FY2028's 6,637, FY2029 and Thereafter remain source-reported buckets, not allocations derived by CP-3 from named instruments or carrying values."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1009","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 116"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The source schedule excludes the separate **487 gross A/R funding** and **262 finance leases**. The A/R facility's **July 11, 2025** date is therefore a separate liquidity/renewal observation, not part of the 93 FY2025 schedule figure. Conditional annual extension rights do not prove extension, but no failure is evidenced either. The 910 revolver commitment maturity on February 27, 2029 is not an additional 910 funded principal maturity. S1 p.45 explicitly reports 67 outstanding letters of credit alongside 843 available; 67 is not inferred drawn borrowing. Live liquidity, cash accessibility and facility conditions remain separate gaps. The **2033 secured notes are 1,500 principal**, not Tranche L's January 2032 exposure or the 2,200 March 2032 secured notes. S1 p.46 reports January 15, 2033 maturity for the 6.000% notes. That annual-reported date is available but does not complete the supplied note form's blank day or substitute for an authenticated issued note, which is Not supplied; coupon dates and call dates do not fill the form. All nine exact annual-reported note dates are retained in the security table above; maturities do not establish call schedules."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1010","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 120"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Debt principal/gross obligations total 25,068, versus accounting carrying debt 24,880. Neither is the complete restructuring claims universe.** The 188 difference is accounting costs/discount effects, not a recovery cushion or forgiveness of creditor claims. The source-based bank/secured-note principal grouping is 19,702 and subordinated-note principal is 4,600; these are descriptive principal pools, not certified pari-passu secured distributions. They omit from that grouping A/R 487, leases 262 and advances 17 while total debt includes them. Calculations and source traces are below."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1011","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 122"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Reach must be evaluated at the **asset-owning and obligor entity**, not by consolidated segment. Inc. has the direct note payment obligation. Holdings and executed guarantors provide separate direct guarantee claims, subject to fraudulent-transfer limits and releases (L \u00a7\u00a710.01\u201310.07, pp.27\u201328). Those guarantees do not create another 1,500 of economic debt for the same 2033 noteholder to recover twice. Non-guarantor creditors have access to local assets before an upstream equity residual reaches note obligors; a restricted subsidiary need not be a guarantor. TransDigm UK is expressly within the executed guarantor structure, so foreign assets cannot all be excluded merely by geography. S1 pp.44\u201345 supplies summarized combined financial data for TD Group, TransDigm Inc. and other guarantors, including TransDigm UK. It excludes non-issuer/non-guarantor subsidiaries, eliminates intercompany balances and transactions among included entities, and separately presents balances/dealings with excluded entities. Guarantor financial information is therefore not wholly absent. This summary does not provide an individual entity/collateral/perfection/value map or an allowed-claims waterfall. Exact entity asset/earnings allocation, residual equity value and solvency limitations remain Not supplied (corrected CP-4 entity register and G06)."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1012","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 124"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The A/R pool is not automatically available to blanket-lien noteholders, and leased assets carry contract-specific rights. Administrative/enforcement costs, accrued interest, potential permitted new or refinancing debt, local trade/employee/tax claims, operating leases and other contingent or statutory claims may affect the distributable pool. Their allowance and priority are jurisdiction- and document-dependent. CP-1 BS13/ND01/LS13 identifies accounts payable 323, current accrued/other liabilities 1,216 and operating leases 62 in 2024; these accounting observations do not supply an allowed-claims waterfall. Do not add the whole balance sheet to principal or double count components embedded in accrued liabilities/debt. No enterprise value, liquidation values, costs-to-realize or allowed claims are supplied, so numeric recoveries and a fulcrum are Not calculable."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1013","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 134"},{"name":"Quote","value":"CP-4's operative findings are material to this comparison: any-RP permission requires no continuing Default/EoD and pro forma legal FCCR **exceeding 2.0x**; permitted commitments may survive later deterioration. Debt permission and lien permission are separate; the **5.25x** secured net ratio belongs to a specific permitted-lien route, not a universal maintenance cap. Projected savings and other legal adjustments can expand transaction capacity without contemporaneous realized cash. These are CP-4 F02\u2013F07 interpretations, not tests computed from CP-1's 4,173 EBITDA As Defined or 6,261 cash. Actual unused baskets, elections, legal EBITDA, eligible cash and the September dividend route remain Not calculable."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1014","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 136"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Counterprotection matters. General majority amendment does **not** establish an unrestricted majority priming right: L \u00a79.02 protects adversely changed ranking/payment terms for affected holders and requires 66\u2154% for specified nonpermitted sweeping collateral release or materially adverse ICA modification (pp.26\u201327, L1834\u2013L1860). Conversely, permitted releases under \u00a7\u00a710.07/12.07 do not necessarily need a new vote. Holders cannot directly enforce Security Documents individually or collectively; agents act under documents and the ICA, which controls conflicts (L pp.29\u201331, \u00a7\u00a711.16,12.01,12.02,12.08). Missing operative ICA standstill, turnover, control votes and purchase options prevent a complete timing/waterfall conclusion. No actual coercive LME, uptier, drop-down, default or perfection failure is established."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1015","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 140"},{"name":"Quote","value":"For **the 6.000% 2033 secured notes only**, L p.15 \u00a73.07 reports ordinary calls at 103.000 in the twelve-month period beginning September 15, 2027, 101.500 in 2028 and 100.000 from 2029, plus accrued interest. Prior redemption uses applicable-premium terms; an equity-offering route permits up to 40% at 106.000 before September 15, 2027, with at least 60% remaining and specified 90-day/purpose conditions. Section 3.08 supplies no scheduled sinking fund and permits open-market purchases. These are contractual prices expressed as percent of principal, not market quotes or predicted exercises. Improved credit/rates may allow refinancing and cap bond price upside, while adverse conditions leave the holder exposed to longer duration. No YTW can be computed without price, complete cash-flow dates and exercise assumptions. None of this call schedule is attributed to the 2028\u20132032 notes or any 2033 instrument other than this supplied 6.000% series."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1016","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 142"},{"name":"Quote","value":"The issuer's 6,261 consolidated cash is **not an unqualified recovery offset**. It precedes the 4,216 accrued common dividend, with October common/equivalent payments 4,216/132 and subsequent A/R draw 162.5 (CP-1 BS01/BS14/SE02/SE03; S1 pp.105,131,146). These later events are not blended into September balances or FY2024 cash flow; no complete post-event cash balance is constructed. Cash may also require entity/location, security, restriction and operating-need analysis. Likewise, reported available revolver 843 is not cash, and nominal A/R capacity 650 less drawn is not certified availability. Carrying leverage remains an accounting analytical ratio, not principal-based recovery coverage or legal headroom."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1017","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 146"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Time-aware operating downside:** from the September 2024 base, weaker utilization or qualified-supplier disruption first reduces spares demand or deliverable shipments (CP-1A B10/B11/B14), then revenue/mix and margin (B04/B08), then collections and inventory conversion (B13; CP-1 K03). Interest, reinvestment and committed payouts compete for cash. Borrowing may initially bridge cash needs but raises claims; eligible A/R may tighten just when liquidity is needed. A July 2025 renewal requirement can matter before longer bond maturities, but no outcome is inferred from the missing follow-up. Notes need not suffer an immediate numerical maintenance breach simply because earnings fall. Transaction incurrence/RP permissions, payment default rules and refinancing access are distinct pathways (CP-4 F01/F13)."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1018","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 148"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Economic loss versus legal loss:** spread widening or rates rising can create mark-to-market loss before any default. Fixed longer notes face duration plus credit-spread repricing; floating loans can have less fixed-rate duration but credit discount and exit-liquidity risk, while higher floating service costs affect issuer cash. In a later restructuring, lower enterprise/pool values, senior dilution, leakage, costs and realization delay reduce distributable proceeds; subordination makes juniors more convex to residual shortfall. A bond's par shortfall is not the investor's entry-price loss: economic loss depends on purchase price, proceeds, interim cash and timing, all of which are missing here. No assumed recovery floor, stress magnitude, PD or portfolio loss is assigned."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1019","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 150"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Economic countercase:** installed-base replacement demand, improving historical conversion and completed extensions may allow retained cash to reduce refinancing dependence. It would win if subsequent comparable financial evidence showed recurring conversion after maintenance/integration needs, actual debt retirement and restrained discretionary payouts. That would improve all claims, potentially letting discounted subordinated debt outperform on price; it still needs verified compensation and residual support."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1020","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 152"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Legal countercase:** guarantees, intended first-priority liens, junior-or-permitted conditions and sacred voting rights may preserve more reachable value than the leakage-risk narrative suggests. It would win if the full executed package, filings, entity map and transaction certificates demonstrate retained collateral, enforceable coverage and constrained competing claims. This would raise conviction in the secured protection case, not mechanically establish its fair spread."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1021","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 154"},{"name":"Quote","value":"**Structural countercase:** a senior label does not ensure superior investment outcome if assets sit in excluded/non-guarantor pools, agents cannot realize value promptly or price already discounts almost no loss. Conversely, enforceable junior guarantees and a sufficiently low entry price could compensate for subordination. Verified entity values, competing claims and comparable prices would decide; missing documents do not prove the adverse structural case. These countercases keep structural preference conditional and implementation withheld rather than converting gaps into Avoid decisions."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1022","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 158"},{"name":"Quote","value":"No portfolio identity, mandate, holdings, NAV, concentration limits, liquidity horizon, leverage/derivative rules, risk budget, eligible-security list or investment clearance is supplied. Therefore no binding portfolio constraint, mandate compliance, numeric sizing, current exposure or proposed pro forma exposure can be established. This is not evidence of a breach or zero capacity. No CLO eligibility is inferred from a loan label, and no loan/commitment is assumed transferable or available to purchase."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id":"C1023","kind":"cited","fields":[{"name":"Source","value":"CP-3"},{"name":"Locator","value":"line 160"},{"name":"Quote","value":"Conditionally, floating secured exposure could suit a vehicle seeking floating income and verified senior asset reach, but it adds rate-service sensitivity, repricing/assignment and liquidity issues. Fixed secured bonds could suit a duration-bearing mandate with sufficient spread compensation and tolerance for call asymmetry. Subordinated exposure requires a mandate able to bear residual-value loss and price volatility, as well as evidence that compensation pays for those risks. Aerospace/defense, issuer, bank/loan and fixed-duration concentrations would have to be measured jointly with existing holdings; reporting segments are not independent correlated-risk buckets. No such category is declared suitable for this unspecified portfolio."},{"name":"SHA-256","value":"d2472fbb0694f2d73882f0c405765c19604dbbf11f5116acc1cbc4c8a01a76d7"}]},{"ref_id"